290
00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:52.100
and ended up falling off a train platform onto the tracks

291
00:09:52.488 --> 00:09:53.902
and got run over by five-
Oh my God.

292
00:09:53.902 --> 00:09:55.174
Subway cars.

293
00:09:55.174 --> 00:09:59.165
And it took one of his legs all the way up to the hip

294
00:09:59.165 --> 00:10:03.111
and the other one mid femur and broke every rib on one side.

295
00:10:03.111 --> 00:10:04.667
And I mean, there's absolutely no,

296
00:10:04.667 --> 00:10:06.084
no logical reason

297
00:10:08.059 --> 00:10:11.725
that he should still be alive after that accident.

298
00:10:11.725 --> 00:10:16.725
But he, you know, he's gone on to not just live a full life,

299
00:10:17.357 --> 00:10:19.801
but a really a fully functional

300
00:10:19.801 --> 00:10:21.720
or more than functional life.

301
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:22.883
And so I'm-
That's amazing.

302
00:10:22.883 --> 00:10:24.999
I'm excited to have some,

303
00:10:24.999 --> 00:10:26.051
you know, company like him.

304
00:10:26.051 --> 00:10:27.187
It's very,

305
00:10:27.187 --> 00:10:28.166
it's very humbling.

306
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:30.055
And I think, again, that he'll,

307
00:10:30.055 --> 00:10:33.514
he's actually gonna attempt this record in a,

308
00:10:33.514 --> 00:10:36.181
on a basically stock wheelchair,

309
00:10:37.223 --> 00:10:39.098
like a street wheelchair.

310
00:10:39.098 --> 00:10:41.758
You're kidding, not with the zip wheels on it

311
00:10:41.758 --> 00:10:42.591
