347
00:12:01.927 --> 00:12:04.011
111 days or something like that, right?

348
00:12:04.011 --> 00:12:05.788
So you've gone more days,

349
00:12:05.788 --> 00:12:09.526
but that was around 40 some odd miles a day, right?

350
00:12:09.526 --> 00:12:11.623
It was gonna be a record

351
00:12:11.623 --> 00:12:13.504
if we could make it all the way across,

352
00:12:13.504 --> 00:12:14.480
which of course we did.

353
00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:15.313
Yeah.

354
00:12:15.313 --> 00:12:16.146
It was going to be a record,

355
00:12:16.146 --> 00:12:19.472
whether it took, you know, 75 days or 150 days,

356
00:12:19.472 --> 00:12:20.631
it would be a record.

357
00:12:20.631 --> 00:12:23.041
So when the inevitable logistical

358
00:12:23.041 --> 00:12:26.148
or physical problems came up,

359
00:12:26.148 --> 00:12:29.859
they didn't really curtail the possibility of the record.

360
00:12:29.859 --> 00:12:32.405
The only thing that would do that would be if,

361
00:12:32.405 --> 00:12:34.313
you know, if Libya hadn't let us-

362
00:12:34.313 --> 00:12:35.670
Right.
In Libya.

363
00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:38.860
In this case, and if we had a bad day in Africa,

364
00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.261
we could, in fact,

