00:18:31.303 --> 00:18:32.993
three days before that run started,

520
00:18:32.993 --> 00:18:37.577
I actually was diagnosed with a staph infection called MRSA.

521
00:18:37.577 --> 00:18:40.006
And I'd never heard of it before.

522
00:18:40.006 --> 00:18:41.160
I didn't even know what it was.

523
00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.901
I'm like, okay, little staph infection.

524
00:18:42.901 --> 00:18:45.786
I'll take some antibiotics.

525
00:18:45.786 --> 00:18:47.524
The doc who was with us actually said,

526
00:18:47.524 --> 00:18:51.024
"Look, you really can't take antibiotics right now.

527
00:18:51.024 --> 00:18:52.972
First of all, they probably won't help.

528
00:18:52.972 --> 00:18:56.333
But if you do, they just destroy your system

529
00:18:56.333 --> 00:18:57.802
and you're getting ready to try to run

530
00:18:57.802 --> 00:19:00.023
70 miles a day."
Right.

531
00:19:00.023 --> 00:19:00.856
So I'm not sure

532
00:19:00.856 --> 00:19:03.544
what I could have done any differently there other than,

533
00:19:03.544 --> 00:19:05.691
not getting the hot tub but

534
00:19:05.691 --> 00:19:07.108
I think that the-

