00:48:42.564 --> 00:48:47.388
but I managed to stay just in front of the curve in that.

1322
00:48:47.388 --> 00:48:51.061
But I joined a fraternity my second year,

1323
00:48:51.061 --> 00:48:53.533
and certainly wasn't their fault.

1324
00:48:53.533 --> 00:48:55.643
They, you know, we would,

1325
00:48:55.643 --> 00:48:56.651
we would party.

1326
00:48:56.651 --> 00:49:00.248
And I was introduced to cocaine at that point.

1327
00:49:00.248 --> 00:49:01.286
It was the '80s though.

1328
00:49:01.286 --> 00:49:02.119
Right.

1329
00:49:02.119 --> 00:49:04.614
It was like, it was ubiquitous.

1330
00:49:04.614 --> 00:49:08.855
It was as common as marijuana like always has been

1331
00:49:08.855 --> 00:49:09.772
or alcohol.

1332
00:49:12.205 --> 00:49:13.078
It just didn't seem,

1333
00:49:13.078 --> 00:49:15.402
it seemed like what everyone else was doing.

1334
00:49:15.402 --> 00:49:19.985
I tried it and it took very little time to realize that

1335
00:49:21.532 --> 00:49:24.038
when I would do it, you know,

1336
00:49:24.038 --> 00:49:27.703
I'm seeing two or three sunrises in a row without sleeping

1337
00:49:27.703 --> 00:49:29.146
while the other guys,

1338
00:49:29.146 --> 00:49:33.763
they might do whatever couple of lines or they might do,

1339
00:49:33.763 --> 00:49:35.148
they might do some.

1340
00:49:35.148 --> 00:49:36.409
And they're actually going to sleep

1341
00:49:36.409 --> 00:49:38.131
at four o'clock in the morning and getting up,

1342
00:49:38.131 --> 00:49:41.192
and going to class or doing whatever it is,

1343
00:49:41.192 --> 00:49:44.640
they were truly the definition of recreational users.

1344
00:49:44.640 --> 00:49:45.473
Right.

1345
00:49:45.473 --> 00:49:46.774
But there's a big difference between

1346
00:49:46.774 --> 00:49:49.486
sort of understanding that like kind of that clicking in

1347
00:49:49.486 --> 00:49:51.281
and going, oh, like I do this a little bit

1348
00:49:51.281 --> 00:49:53.492
differently than everyone else.

1349
00:49:53.492 --> 00:49:55.434
I mean, a normal person would say,

1350
00:49:55.434 --> 00:49:58.587
well, that's when you start to rectify this situation.

1351
00:49:58.587 --> 00:50:01.781
But I know for myself very early on,

1352
00:50:01.781 --> 00:50:03.935
I was like, I'm definitely an alcoholic,

1353
00:50:03.935 --> 00:50:07.255
but I would never admit that I knew in my heart of hearts,

1354
00:50:07.255 --> 00:50:10.026
but I was 'cause I knew that I drank differently

1355
00:50:10.026 --> 00:50:12.826
and I have a huge scar on my leg from a lost weekend

1356
00:50:12.826 --> 00:50:14.743
I spent at UNC in 1986.

1357
00:50:15.707 --> 00:50:16.915
(Rich laughing)

1358
00:50:16.915 --> 00:50:18.030
Was I there?

1359
00:50:18.030 --> 00:50:19.269
Where I woke up at, I don't know,

1360
00:50:19.269 --> 00:50:21.253
maybe, maybe we partied together.

1361
00:50:21.253 --> 00:50:22.115
(Charlie laughing)

1362
00:50:22.115 --> 00:50:23.453
Were you there in eight, yeah.

1363
00:50:23.453 --> 00:50:25.799
Wait, did I hit you with an ax handle?

1364
00:50:25.799 --> 00:50:26.906
Yeah, maybe.

1365
00:50:26.906 --> 00:50:28.888
Maybe you caused the scar on my leg.

1366
00:50:28.888 --> 00:50:29.721
I wouldn't be surprised.

1367
00:50:29.721 --> 00:50:31.353
(Charlie laughing)

1368
00:50:31.353 --> 00:50:34.864
But what happened to me was that that set in motion,

1369
00:50:34.864 --> 00:50:38.531
a chain of events to protect my future right

1370
00:50:39.969 --> 00:50:41.147
to continue to use.

1371
00:50:41.147 --> 00:50:44.001
It's like, oh, well, hmm, you know, I better,

1372
00:50:44.001 --> 00:50:45.853
I better really kind of watch myself

1373
00:50:45.853 --> 00:50:48.186
because I wanna continue to be able to do this.

1374
00:50:48.186 --> 00:50:49.798
So if it gets too outta control too soon,

1375
00:50:49.798 --> 00:50:51.448
then I'm gonna have to do something about it

1376
00:50:51.448 --> 00:50:52.281
or I'm gonna have,

1377
00:50:52.281 --> 00:50:53.484
somebody else is gonna tell me

1378
00:50:53.484 --> 00:50:55.398
I have to do something about it.

1379
00:50:55.398 --> 00:50:57.893
So it was all about trying to preserve your ability

1380
00:50:57.893 --> 00:51:00.359
to continue to be able to party.

1381
00:51:00.359 --> 00:51:03.197
And, of course, never being able to get that balance right,

1382
00:51:03.197 --> 00:51:04.431
or that mix right.

1383
00:51:04.431 --> 00:51:08.015
And it just continues to get worse and spiral outta control.

1384
00:51:08.015 --> 00:51:09.987
Well, I went to my first AA meeting

1385
00:51:09.987 --> 00:51:12.313
when I was 23 years old in Atlanta.

1386
00:51:12.313 --> 00:51:13.146
Right.

1387
00:51:13.146 --> 00:51:15.631
And I didn't get clean and sober until I was 29.

1388
00:51:15.631 --> 00:51:16.760
So that tells you something.

1389
00:51:16.760 --> 00:51:19.280
And so the acknowledgement of the problem.

1390
00:51:19.280 --> 00:51:20.165
Right.

1391
00:51:20.165 --> 00:51:22.470
Was there very early on.

1392
00:51:22.470 --> 00:51:24.275
Self-knowledge will avail you nothing.

1393
00:51:24.275 --> 00:51:25.239
Yeah, and right,

1394
00:51:25.239 --> 00:51:26.322
exactly right.
(Rich laughing)

1395
00:51:26.322 --> 00:51:29.255
And I absolutely kept fighting it and kept,

1396
00:51:29.255 --> 00:51:32.559
you know, of course, I changed my,

1397
00:51:32.559 --> 00:51:34.728
my plan a thousand times,

1398
00:51:34.728 --> 00:51:37.430
I'm not going to do drugs.

1399
00:51:37.430 --> 00:51:38.263
Right.

1400
00:51:38.263 --> 00:51:39.096
I'm just gonna drink.

1401
00:51:39.096 --> 00:51:39.929
I'm not gonna drink liquor.

1402
00:51:39.929 --> 00:51:41.181
I'm just gonna drink beer.

1403
00:51:41.181 --> 00:51:42.791
I mean, whatever it might be.

1404
00:51:42.791 --> 00:51:43.645
I did it.

1405
00:51:43.645 --> 00:51:47.895
I did at least seven or eight geographical changes,

1406
00:51:48.869 --> 00:51:50.759
which is common for addicts.

1407
00:51:50.759 --> 00:51:51.592
Right.

1408
00:51:51.592 --> 00:51:53.052
Where I would go somewhere

1409
00:51:53.052 --> 00:51:55.303
and I'd move to Seattle and get a new job

1410
00:51:55.303 --> 00:51:58.158
and a new girlfriend and a, you know,

1411
00:51:58.158 --> 00:52:01.004
life would be fantastic for six months.

1412
00:52:01.004 --> 00:52:02.447
Then you wake up and you go,

1413
00:52:02.447 --> 00:52:04.513
oh, shit, I brought myself with me.

1414
00:52:04.513 --> 00:52:05.761
I gotta move again.

1415
00:52:05.761 --> 00:52:06.594
Darn it.
(Rich laughing)

1416
00:52:06.594 --> 00:52:07.610
You know, and that would,

1417
00:52:07.610 --> 00:52:09.220
that would be what would happen is then,

1418
00:52:09.220 --> 00:52:11.472
within a year I'd be off to some other city

1419
00:52:11.472 --> 00:52:13.040
to do it better.

1420
00:52:13.040 --> 00:52:15.992
And, of course, do it exactly the same the next time,

1421
00:52:15.992 --> 00:52:18.567
because sure enough, there I was.

1422
00:52:18.567 --> 00:52:22.950
And it just took what it took the last time.

1423
00:52:22.950 --> 00:52:25.301
Yeah, the last time was

1424
00:52:25.301 --> 00:52:27.497
at least the last time up to now, as we say-

1425
00:52:27.497 --> 00:52:28.330
Yeah.

1426
00:52:28.330 --> 00:52:30.399
It was over 21 years ago,

1427
00:52:30.399 --> 00:52:32.110
and it was very memorable-

1428
00:52:32.110 --> 00:52:33.105
Because you and I are gonna go,

1429
00:52:33.105 --> 00:52:34.152
we're gonna go-
we're gonna go

1430
00:52:34.152 --> 00:52:35.322
hammered right after this.

1431
00:52:35.322 --> 00:52:36.835
Yeah, right after we finish the podcast.

1432
00:52:36.835 --> 00:52:38.308
(Charlie laughing)
(Rich laughing)

1433
00:52:38.308 --> 00:52:39.416
People ask me every year.

1434
00:52:39.416 --> 00:52:40.424
Why wait until we're done?

1435
00:52:40.424 --> 00:52:42.216
Let's see what we have in the cabinet.

1436
00:52:42.216 --> 00:52:43.236
People ask me every year,

1437
00:52:43.236 --> 00:52:45.910
they're like, I'll tell 'em, that's my sobriety birthday.

1438
00:52:45.910 --> 00:52:47.762
Like I don't celebrate my regular birthday.

1439
00:52:47.762 --> 00:52:48.595
Yeah.

1440
00:52:48.595 --> 00:52:49.888
But I celebrate my sobriety birthday.

1441
00:52:49.888 --> 00:52:50.721
What are you gonna do?

1442
00:52:50.721 --> 00:52:52.281
I'm like, I'm gonna go get shit-faced.

1443
00:52:52.281 --> 00:52:53.114
Right.

1444
00:52:53.114 --> 00:52:55.079
And they'll look at me like, "Really?"

1445
00:52:55.079 --> 00:52:56.729
I'm like, no, I'm not, but-

1446
00:52:56.729 --> 00:52:58.246
Well, people would be amazed

1447
00:52:58.246 --> 00:53:00.863
how many people relapse on their first year anniversary?

1448
00:53:00.863 --> 00:53:01.816
Oh yeah.

1449
00:53:01.816 --> 00:53:03.415
Because only the alcoholic will think

1450
00:53:03.415 --> 00:53:05.679
it's a good idea to celebrate a year of sobriety

1451
00:53:05.679 --> 00:53:06.523
by getting drunk.

1452
00:53:06.523 --> 00:53:07.356
Yeah.

1453
00:53:07.356 --> 00:53:09.051
You know, that makes perfect sense to me.

1454
00:53:09.051 --> 00:53:09.896
Well, clearly they've proven

1455
00:53:09.896 --> 00:53:10.729
(Rich laughing)

1456
00:53:10.729 --> 00:53:12.209
that they're drink like a normal person now.

1457
00:53:12.209 --> 00:53:13.042
Yeah.

1458
00:53:13.042 --> 00:53:13.988
So-
Right.

1459
00:53:13.988 --> 00:53:14.923
Yeah, I messed it up.

1460
00:53:14.923 --> 00:53:17.423
I'm messed up, you know, jobs,

1461
00:53:19.124 --> 00:53:23.005
and certainly my own life and wasted a lot of time.

1462
00:53:23.005 --> 00:53:24.607
I mean, I did my first,

1463
00:53:24.607 --> 00:53:27.713
my first three marathons I ever did,

1464
00:53:27.713 --> 00:53:32.380
really my first four were still when I was very unsober.

1465
00:53:33.521 --> 00:53:35.268
I'll never forget in fact,

1466
00:53:35.268 --> 00:53:39.731
doing my first marathon, which was Big Sur back in 1989.

1467
00:53:39.731 --> 00:53:42.547
And I mean, I did enter the race until about a week

1468
00:53:42.547 --> 00:53:46.328
before the race, did essentially no training,

1469
00:53:46.328 --> 00:53:48.021
but I'd been out doing some running,

1470
00:53:48.021 --> 00:53:51.771
and I just decided that this was another way.

1471
00:53:52.863 --> 00:53:54.043
This was how I could prove.

1472
00:53:54.043 --> 00:53:55.235
Clearly I'm not an alcoholic or an addict-

1473
00:53:55.235 --> 00:53:56.068
Right.

1474
00:53:56.068 --> 00:53:56.901
If I can go out and-

1475
00:53:56.901 --> 00:53:57.738
Exactly.
And do a marathon.

1476
00:53:57.738 --> 00:53:59.288
So I enter this-
Yeah.

1477
00:53:59.288 --> 00:54:02.371
Enter this race and I go,

1478
00:54:03.421 --> 00:54:05.679
and I do actually finish the thing.

1479
00:54:05.679 --> 00:54:07.858
And in a decent, you know,

1480
00:54:07.858 --> 00:54:09.594
I think three and a half hour time,

1481
00:54:09.594 --> 00:54:11.683
having no idea what I was doing

1482
00:54:11.683 --> 00:54:14.072
and Bur Sur was a fairly hard marathon.

1483
00:54:14.072 --> 00:54:17.559
And I get to the finish line and I'm looking around,

1484
00:54:17.559 --> 00:54:20.960
there's all these people hugging and crying.

1485
00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:24.710
And they're like, I mean, this amazing thing.

1486
00:54:26.752 --> 00:54:28.925
I make the joke, if anybody watches Dexter,

1487
00:54:28.925 --> 00:54:30.717
it's like Dexter trying to figure out,

1488
00:54:30.717 --> 00:54:33.955
when he is watching other people have emotions

1489
00:54:33.955 --> 00:54:36.245
and, you know, he is trying to figure out

1490
00:54:36.245 --> 00:54:37.970
not only why he doesn't feel that way,

1491
00:54:37.970 --> 00:54:39.088
but how to fake it.

1492
00:54:39.088 --> 00:54:39.921
Right.

1493
00:54:39.921 --> 00:54:40.754
And, you know,

1494
00:54:40.754 --> 00:54:43.335
like I desperately wanted to find somebody to hug and cry

1495
00:54:43.335 --> 00:54:47.338
so that I could feel fantastic about what I'd just done.

1496
00:54:47.338 --> 00:54:49.393
And instead, I just went out and got drunk that night.

1497
00:54:49.393 --> 00:54:51.731
Right, and you bring up an important point,

1498
00:54:51.731 --> 00:54:53.397
which is this idea.

1499
00:54:53.397 --> 00:54:54.266
And I relate to the,

1500
00:54:54.266 --> 00:54:56.742
I used to do this all the time.

1501
00:54:56.742 --> 00:54:58.370
This false pride that takes over.

1502
00:54:58.370 --> 00:54:59.664
Like you test yourself,

1503
00:54:59.664 --> 00:55:01.812
say, well, if I can go out and run this marathon,

1504
00:55:01.812 --> 00:55:03.614
I can just bang out these marathons on the weekend.

1505
00:55:03.614 --> 00:55:05.339
Then I must not have a drinking problem.

1506
00:55:05.339 --> 00:55:09.256
It's artillery to sort of use it as you will to

1507
00:55:13.803 --> 00:55:16.091
continue to be able to justify your drinking

1508
00:55:16.091 --> 00:55:17.081
and using, right?

1509
00:55:17.081 --> 00:55:19.253
And also like, "Hey, look what I did."

1510
00:55:19.253 --> 00:55:21.674
Like not only did I run,

1511
00:55:21.674 --> 00:55:23.548
I went out, I got completely shift-faced.

1512
00:55:23.548 --> 00:55:26.059
I woke up, I was hung over and I still ran a marathon.

1513
00:55:26.059 --> 00:55:27.571
Like, what did you do this weekend?

1514
00:55:27.571 --> 00:55:28.404
You know what I mean?

1515
00:55:28.404 --> 00:55:30.354
And it's like, there's no humility in that.

1516
00:55:30.354 --> 00:55:34.052
There's a complete false pride thing that takes over

1517
00:55:34.052 --> 00:55:37.258
that leads you in a very dark direction ultimately.

1518
00:55:37.258 --> 00:55:39.651
I was at the end of those first few marathons,

1519
00:55:39.651 --> 00:55:41.866
I could not have been emptier,

1520
00:55:41.866 --> 00:55:43.211
and it actually even goes back

1521
00:55:43.211 --> 00:55:44.786
to what we were talking about before,

1522
00:55:44.786 --> 00:55:46.819
'cause I had the raw emotion,

1523
00:55:46.819 --> 00:55:48.177
like I'd done this work.

1524
00:55:48.177 --> 00:55:52.138
And I had indeed scraped off those outer layers

1525
00:55:52.138 --> 00:55:56.043
to find that I was absolutely completely empty inside

1526
00:55:56.043 --> 00:55:58.543
and at least drugs and alcohol

1527
00:55:59.757 --> 00:56:02.897
gave some texture to the emptiness

1528
00:56:02.897 --> 00:56:05.306
and then being, you know, having that,

1529
00:56:05.306 --> 00:56:06.639
not as a crotch,

1530
00:56:09.629 --> 00:56:11.827
really was something I couldn't imagine at the time.

1531
00:56:11.827 --> 00:56:12.660
And I was doing,

1532
00:56:12.660 --> 00:56:16.007
I was at 25 or 6, you know, I wanted to like,

1533
00:56:16.007 --> 00:56:18.714
I think I bought my first house right around there,

1534
00:56:18.714 --> 00:56:21.628
and I bought cars and I wanted to be and was

1535
00:56:21.628 --> 00:56:24.546
like the top salesman at whatever job I was doing.

1536
00:56:24.546 --> 00:56:27.703
And those were all nothing more than my

1537
00:56:27.703 --> 00:56:31.999
proof that clearly there can't be any kind of a problem

1538
00:56:31.999 --> 00:56:34.054
if I can do those things,

1539
00:56:34.054 --> 00:56:36.623
then, you know, how could I possibly have a problem?

1540
00:56:36.623 --> 00:56:37.456
Right.

1541
00:56:37.456 --> 00:56:41.199
And that looming sense of emptiness is so terrifying

1542
00:56:41.199 --> 00:56:43.470
that the only way to deal with it is to

1543
00:56:43.470 --> 00:56:44.644
drink more and use more.

1544
00:56:44.644 --> 00:56:45.477
Fill it.

1545
00:56:45.477 --> 00:56:47.694
I could fill it up that way at least temporarily.

1546
00:56:47.694 --> 00:56:48.527
Right.

1547
00:56:48.527 --> 00:56:49.724
And that's of course,

1548
00:56:49.724 --> 00:56:52.474
what we all do in that situation.

1549
00:56:53.555 --> 00:56:55.403
And, you know, and it taught me,

1550
00:56:55.403 --> 00:56:56.346
it did teach me,

1551
00:56:56.346 --> 00:57:00.916
I will say it did teach me how to suffer properly.

1552
00:57:00.916 --> 00:57:03.195
The things I did to myself then

1553
00:57:03.195 --> 00:57:04.695
that's true suffering.

1554
00:57:04.695 --> 00:57:07.438
And when I'm out running

1555
00:57:07.438 --> 00:57:10.818
and whether I'm falling apart or having a great run,

1556
00:57:10.818 --> 00:57:13.527
I mean, even races like Badwater,

1557
00:57:13.527 --> 00:57:15.710
people tend to think that, oh, you did it.

1558
00:57:15.710 --> 00:57:19.154
And you had a good time and like a good finishing time

1559
00:57:19.154 --> 00:57:20.465
and you placed well and whatever.

1560
00:57:20.465 --> 00:57:22.064
So you had a fantastic race.

1561
00:57:22.064 --> 00:57:25.096
Like somehow that means that you didn't struggle

1562
00:57:25.096 --> 00:57:25.937
during the race-
Yeah.

1563
00:57:25.937 --> 00:57:29.141
And like Badwater is a race that,

1564
00:57:29.141 --> 00:57:31.494
I've never not thrown up at Badwater.

1565
00:57:31.494 --> 00:57:33.934
It's the only race I've ever thrown up in, in fact,

1566
00:57:33.934 --> 00:57:35.780
but I've done it every single time.

1567
00:57:35.780 --> 00:57:38.554
Like something about the heat mechanism there.

1568
00:57:38.554 --> 00:57:42.236
And just the point being that there's a series of ups

1569
00:57:42.236 --> 00:57:45.274
and downs during that race that are inevitable

1570
00:57:45.274 --> 00:57:47.679
and no matter how I plan,

1571
00:57:47.679 --> 00:57:49.147
they're going to happen,

1572
00:57:49.147 --> 00:57:50.393
those downs.

1573
00:57:50.393 --> 00:57:52.455
And that's what I finally had to understand.

1574
00:57:52.455 --> 00:57:55.466
Well, it's what I've had to understand about sobriety.

1575
00:57:55.466 --> 00:57:56.612
And so over 21 years,

1576
00:57:56.612 --> 00:57:58.974
I didn't stop me from going to prison a couple of years ago.

1577
00:57:58.974 --> 00:57:59.827
Right.

1578
00:57:59.827 --> 00:58:00.776
You know, it didn't,

1579
00:58:00.776 --> 00:58:03.949
it didn't stop my first marriage from falling apart.

1580
00:58:03.949 --> 00:58:05.498
It didn't stop,

1581
00:58:05.498 --> 00:58:06.415
didn't stop anything.

1582
00:58:06.415 --> 00:58:08.776
Life just continued to roll on.

1583
00:58:08.776 --> 00:58:11.346
It's just that I actually had to be present for it,

1584
00:58:11.346 --> 00:58:12.763
which was really.

1585
00:58:12.763 --> 00:58:13.596
You had to feel it.

1586
00:58:13.596 --> 00:58:14.429
Yeah.

1587
00:58:14.429 --> 00:58:15.970
Damn.

1588
00:58:15.970 --> 00:58:17.802
It's sort of that idea that,

1589
00:58:17.802 --> 00:58:21.295
sobriety doesn't promise you anything other than

1590
00:58:21.295 --> 00:58:23.311
