2392
01:27:21.492 --> 01:27:22.325
(Rich laughing)

2393
01:27:22.325 --> 01:27:24.480
And I wrote, he gave some reasons and I wrote him back.

2394
01:27:24.480 --> 01:27:26.555
I said, I said, "Dude, I couldn't agree with you more."

2395
01:27:26.555 --> 01:27:27.388
(Rich laughing)

2396
01:27:27.388 --> 01:27:32.388
I said, but just realize that it's not always exactly,

2397
01:27:32.460 --> 01:27:34.209
exactly what you see and that's the way everything is.

2398
01:27:34.209 --> 01:27:35.042
Right, right.

2399
01:27:35.042 --> 01:27:36.944
That's the way, that's the way prison was.

2400
01:27:36.944 --> 01:27:39.838
That's again, I'm hoping that in writing,

2401
01:27:39.838 --> 01:27:41.588
I can tell that story

2402
01:27:42.859 --> 01:27:44.692
in a way that doesn't,

2403
01:27:46.108 --> 01:27:47.367
I don't wanna bore anybody

2404
01:27:47.367 --> 01:27:51.227
and we're not gonna go into all the details in the book of,

2405
01:27:51.227 --> 01:27:55.228
every minuscule thing that happened at trial or in prison.

2406
01:27:55.228 --> 01:27:57.547
But the book is really gonna be a running book

2407
01:27:57.547 --> 01:27:58.380
more than anything.

2408
01:27:58.380 --> 01:28:01.579
But I mean, there is room to kind of talk about all of that.

2409
01:28:01.579 --> 01:28:03.289
Right, so the working title is

2410
01:28:03.289 --> 01:28:04.482
"Running Unempty"

2411
01:28:04.482 --> 01:28:05.328
Running In Place."

2412
01:28:05.328 --> 01:28:06.161
"Running In Place."

2413
01:28:06.161 --> 01:28:07.109
Sorry.
Yeah.

2414
01:28:07.109 --> 01:28:08.965
And I had the great privilege of reading

2415
01:28:08.965 --> 01:28:12.909
the proposal and some of the sample materials,

2416
01:28:12.909 --> 01:28:14.702
the sample chapters that you've already prepared

2417
01:28:14.702 --> 01:28:16.562
and it's a barn burner.

2418
01:28:16.562 --> 01:28:17.896
When I first reached out to you,

2419
01:28:17.896 --> 01:28:19.264
I think I even said on Twitter,

2420
01:28:19.264 --> 01:28:21.494
I was like, I can't wait to read this guy's book.

2421
01:28:21.494 --> 01:28:22.728
Like this is the book,

2422
01:28:22.728 --> 01:28:24.076
like if you like "Finding Ultra,"

2423
01:28:24.076 --> 01:28:27.091
this is like "Finding Ultra" on steroids times a billion,

2424
01:28:27.091 --> 01:28:30.694
like the epic tale of Gilgamesh or something,

2425
01:28:30.694 --> 01:28:33.085
but I'm interested in where you're at right now

2426
01:28:33.085 --> 01:28:34.335
in the process.

2427
01:28:35.206 --> 01:28:37.087
How long is it gonna be?

2428
01:28:37.087 --> 01:28:39.504
And kind of the trajectory of

2429
01:28:40.548 --> 01:28:42.502
how you're gonna get this book done and out.

2430
01:28:42.502 --> 01:28:45.752
I've got a fantastic agent,

2431
01:28:46.850 --> 01:28:51.169
with the help of a professional team really,

2432
01:28:51.169 --> 01:28:52.727
we managed to put out a,

2433
01:28:52.727 --> 01:28:54.975
I think what is a really good proposal,

2434
01:28:54.975 --> 01:28:57.398
and that proposal is actually out to publishers just-

2435
01:28:57.398 --> 01:28:58.472
Oh, you went out with it already.

2436
01:28:58.472 --> 01:28:59.569
Just now literally.

2437
01:28:59.569 --> 01:29:00.402
Oh, cool.

2438
01:29:00.402 --> 01:29:01.235
Literally just now.

2439
01:29:01.235 --> 01:29:02.068
Oh, that's exciting.

2440
01:29:02.068 --> 01:29:03.655
And we've had a couple of great responses already.

2441
01:29:03.655 --> 01:29:04.488
Fantastic.

2442
01:29:04.488 --> 01:29:06.988
And I'm hoping that in the very near future,

2443
01:29:06.988 --> 01:29:09.969
there'll be an announcement to be made that,

2444
01:29:09.969 --> 01:29:11.782
you know, then it's like,

2445
01:29:11.782 --> 01:29:12.615
it's kinda like,

2446
01:29:12.615 --> 01:29:13.843
it's kind of like entering a race though,

2447
01:29:13.843 --> 01:29:15.173
then I actually have to write it.

2448
01:29:15.173 --> 01:29:16.006
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2449
01:29:16.006 --> 01:29:16.839
Which as you know.

2450
01:29:16.839 --> 01:29:18.275
I know.
Is-

2451
01:29:18.275 --> 01:29:19.528
Just one day at a time.

2452
01:29:19.528 --> 01:29:20.740
I wrote about,

2453
01:29:20.740 --> 01:29:22.382
I think I wrote about a thousand pages

2454
01:29:22.382 --> 01:29:23.928
when I was at Beckley.

2455
01:29:23.928 --> 01:29:28.161
So if I could just transfer all that over,

2456
01:29:28.161 --> 01:29:29.613
and it was useful, that'd be great.

2457
01:29:29.613 --> 01:29:31.560
But again as you know that's not the way the-

2458
01:29:31.560 --> 01:29:33.371
Yeah, but at least you don't,

2459
01:29:33.371 --> 01:29:34.204
Process works.

2460
01:29:34.204 --> 01:29:35.037
But it's not a,

2461
01:29:35.037 --> 01:29:35.870
you're not staring at a blank page,

2462
01:29:35.870 --> 01:29:37.309
you have all this material to work with.

2463
01:29:37.309 --> 01:29:38.142
I've done enough.

2464
01:29:38.142 --> 01:29:39.261
It's not like you don't know the story either.

2465
01:29:39.261 --> 01:29:40.094
Yeah, it's mine.

2466
01:29:40.094 --> 01:29:40.927
I can't really be wrong.

2467
01:29:40.927 --> 01:29:41.760
(Rich laughing)

2468
01:29:41.760 --> 01:29:42.593
Can I?

2469
01:29:43.547 --> 01:29:45.384
The question is, can I make it compelling?

2470
01:29:45.384 --> 01:29:47.384
And I like to think that

2471
01:29:48.868 --> 01:29:50.462
that it'll be,

2472
01:29:50.462 --> 01:29:53.234
I'm here to say as always that,

2473
01:29:53.234 --> 01:29:55.782
that it's a work in progress and so am I,

2474
01:29:55.782 --> 01:29:59.782
and there, I will never have all the answers to,

2475
01:30:01.441 --> 01:30:02.856
who I am and why I do things.

2476
01:30:02.856 --> 01:30:05.792
And I don't think any of us do.

2477
01:30:05.792 --> 01:30:10.514
And if I quit asking those questions, then I'm in trouble.

2478
01:30:10.514 --> 01:30:13.510
I'll tell you something actually,

2479
01:30:13.510 --> 01:30:17.959
Astacianna, who I'm lucky enough to be marrying on Saturday.

2480
01:30:17.959 --> 01:30:19.567
Ask me one of the hardest questions,

2481
01:30:19.567 --> 01:30:21.859
I've ever been asked,

2482
01:30:21.859 --> 01:30:23.713
at one of our first dates,

2483
01:30:23.713 --> 01:30:28.455
and she sort of looked at me probably wisely wondering,

2484
01:30:28.455 --> 01:30:31.422
what was going on with me?

2485
01:30:31.422 --> 01:30:35.255
And because there's all these tales of misery,

2486
01:30:36.667 --> 01:30:39.664
I'm good at overcoming the difficult things,

2487
01:30:39.664 --> 01:30:42.096
and putting myself sometimes,

2488
01:30:42.096 --> 01:30:43.805
some of the things I did myself,

2489
01:30:43.805 --> 01:30:45.658
some were done to me,

2490
01:30:45.658 --> 01:30:47.165
which is like most of us

2491
01:30:47.165 --> 01:30:48.834
and some things just happen

2492
01:30:48.834 --> 01:30:52.167
and I'm good at setting my mind to that.

2493
01:30:53.590 --> 01:30:55.807
But she asked me the question,

2494
01:30:55.807 --> 01:30:58.724
do I have any clue how to be happy?

2495
01:31:00.261 --> 01:31:01.725
Like how to just be happy?

2496
01:31:01.725 --> 01:31:04.523
Like if things were going fantastically,

2497
01:31:04.523 --> 01:31:06.455
could I just be happy?

2498
01:31:06.455 --> 01:31:10.247
And I thought it was the most amazing question ever

2499
01:31:10.247 --> 01:31:11.813
because I realized right away

2500
01:31:11.813 --> 01:31:14.641
that really the answer to that question was no,

2501
01:31:14.641 --> 01:31:17.180
I've never really understood

2502
01:31:17.180 --> 01:31:18.930
like how to be happy.

2503
01:31:19.847 --> 01:31:22.847
And I'm hoping that there's,

2504
01:31:22.847 --> 01:31:26.695
that there's that ability's gonna grow in me,

2505
01:31:26.695 --> 01:31:30.528
certainly with her, it will be forced to grow.

2506
01:31:31.665 --> 01:31:34.004
'Cause she's much better at it than I am,

2507
01:31:34.004 --> 01:31:37.185
but it's an interesting thing,

2508
01:31:37.185 --> 01:31:39.618
I think maybe I've relied on suffering

2509
01:31:39.618 --> 01:31:42.202
and my desire somehow to suffer

2510
01:31:42.202 --> 01:31:45.866
and find my discovery through suffering,

2511
01:31:45.866 --> 01:31:49.016
that that's the way I've always functioned and so.

2512
01:31:49.016 --> 01:31:50.047
Well, you have,

2513
01:31:50.047 --> 01:31:51.978
you have alcoholism, it's the ism.

2514
01:31:51.978 --> 01:31:52.811
Yeah.

2515
01:31:52.811 --> 01:31:53.729
It's the I seek misery.

2516
01:31:53.729 --> 01:31:54.562
Yeah.
Right?

2517
01:31:54.562 --> 01:31:56.415
But happiness,

2518
01:31:56.415 --> 01:31:58.665
happiness, I don't think is

2519
01:31:59.746 --> 01:32:01.116
a destination.

2520
01:32:01.116 --> 01:32:02.544
It's a process.

2521
01:32:02.544 --> 01:32:03.810
And I think it, you know,

2522
01:32:03.810 --> 01:32:06.810
I think that you get glimpses of it,

2523
01:32:07.711 --> 01:32:11.091
or I get glimpses of it when you can get out of yourself

2524
01:32:11.091 --> 01:32:12.189
and be of service.

2525
01:32:12.189 --> 01:32:15.687
And when you're tapped into somebody that you care about

2526
01:32:15.687 --> 01:32:20.169
and when you are expressing yourself authentically,

2527
01:32:20.169 --> 01:32:23.401
and I think that in terms of your book,

2528
01:32:23.401 --> 01:32:27.027
if all you do is share your experience

2529
01:32:27.027 --> 01:32:29.982
and you do it honestly with integrity

2530
01:32:29.982 --> 01:32:31.494
and you allow yourself to be

2531
01:32:31.494 --> 01:32:33.986
vulnerable in that process,

2532
01:32:33.986 --> 01:32:35.505
that it will be difficult

2533
01:32:35.505 --> 01:32:38.577
and you will suffer just like you do in an ultra,

2534
01:32:38.577 --> 01:32:40.740
but there will be a sense of satisfaction.

2535
01:32:40.740 --> 01:32:42.584
And I think we talk a lot about happiness,

2536
01:32:42.584 --> 01:32:43.816
but it's really about like,

2537
01:32:43.816 --> 01:32:45.879
are you gonna be a satisfied human?

2538
01:32:45.879 --> 01:32:47.483
I think that's more of,

2539
01:32:47.483 --> 01:32:49.936
that's a better sort of inquiry,

2540
01:32:49.936 --> 01:32:52.208
or one, at least I can relate to a little bit more.

2541
01:32:52.208 --> 01:32:54.541
I agree.

2542
01:32:54.541 --> 01:32:57.285
The fear, although it's not rational,

2543
01:32:57.285 --> 01:32:58.532
but it doesn't have to be rational.

2544
01:32:58.532 --> 01:33:01.419
The fear is somehow that if I'm a content,

2545
01:33:01.419 --> 01:33:03.553
like even for five minutes,

2546
01:33:03.553 --> 01:33:05.202
that I'm gonna lose some edge-

2547
01:33:05.202 --> 01:33:06.035
Right.
(Rich laughing)

2548
01:33:06.035 --> 01:33:06.982
Like the, oh my God,

2549
01:33:06.982 --> 01:33:08.026
now I'm gonna sit on the sofa

2550
01:33:08.026 --> 01:33:10.892
and eat popcorn for the rest of my life,

2551
01:33:10.892 --> 01:33:13.110
And that would just be terrible.

2552
01:33:13.110 --> 01:33:14.630
And it's finding, it is,

2553
01:33:14.630 --> 01:33:16.881
it's trying to find some sort of a balance

2554
01:33:16.881 --> 01:33:19.722
where I can enjoy myself.

2555
01:33:19.722 --> 01:33:21.555
I can enjoy just being

2556
01:33:22.912 --> 01:33:25.258
and not always be looking forward

2557
01:33:25.258 --> 01:33:27.563
to whatever that next thing is.

2558
01:33:27.563 --> 01:33:28.539
And I, you know,

2559
01:33:28.539 --> 01:33:29.372
I vowed

2560
01:33:30.927 --> 01:33:33.348
now, you know, that when Run2Boston

2561
01:33:33.348 --> 01:33:35.959
is finished this year,

2562
