in helping them change their own life,

2624
01:35:30.458 --> 01:35:31.600
whether it was losing weight,

2625
01:35:31.600 --> 01:35:32.850
or just running

2626
01:35:34.355 --> 01:35:38.522
or, working out or changing their attitude towards

2627
01:35:39.863 --> 01:35:40.978
how they ate.

2628
01:35:40.978 --> 01:35:42.689
I mean, even in prison, you know-

2629
01:35:42.689 --> 01:35:43.665
Right.

2630
01:35:43.665 --> 01:35:45.291
You've got this issue with eating all the time.

2631
01:35:45.291 --> 01:35:47.208
I don't know, it was just really,

2632
01:35:47.208 --> 01:35:48.731
it was wonderful.

2633
01:35:48.731 --> 01:35:51.803
Well, I think what's great about that is-

2634
01:35:51.803 --> 01:35:52.636
By the way-
It relates-

2635
01:35:52.636 --> 01:35:54.096
I don't wanna do it again, by the way.

2636
01:35:54.096 --> 01:35:54.929
No, yeah.
(Rich laughing)

2637
01:35:54.929 --> 01:35:55.762
Just to be clear.

2638
01:35:55.762 --> 01:35:56.849
Let's try to, yeah,

2639
01:35:56.849 --> 01:35:57.682
let's try to one way that,

2640
01:35:57.682 --> 01:35:59.236
right?
Okay, right.

2641
01:35:59.236 --> 01:36:00.069
What I loved about it though,

2642
01:36:00.069 --> 01:36:03.305
was that it really was this kind of,

2643
01:36:03.305 --> 01:36:07.409
using the principles of recovery in that,

2644
01:36:07.409 --> 01:36:08.857
you referenced it earlier,

2645
01:36:08.857 --> 01:36:11.607
it's a program of attraction not-

2646
01:36:14.300 --> 01:36:15.203
Promotion.

2647
01:36:15.203 --> 01:36:16.154
Promotion or recruitment.

2648
01:36:16.154 --> 01:36:17.905
And so you would just go out and run every day

2649
01:36:17.905 --> 01:36:18.890
and you weren't like trying to

2650
01:36:18.890 --> 01:36:20.355
get anyone else to go with you.

2651
01:36:20.355 --> 01:36:21.483
You're like, this is what I'm doing.

2652
01:36:21.483 --> 01:36:22.396
And then slowly,

2653
01:36:22.396 --> 01:36:23.978
these guys are starting to show up

2654
01:36:23.978 --> 01:36:25.140
and I love the characters.

2655
01:36:25.140 --> 01:36:28.937
They're like Butter Bean and Bootsy and Block.

2656
01:36:28.937 --> 01:36:29.911
And these guys-

2657
01:36:29.911 --> 01:36:30.744
Yeah.

2658
01:36:30.744 --> 01:36:33.212
You know, from what I can understand,

2659
01:36:33.212 --> 01:36:34.672
like the furthest thing from

2660
01:36:34.672 --> 01:36:35.954
being an athlete or being run

2661
01:36:35.954 --> 01:36:37.745
or some of them tremendously overweight.

2662
01:36:37.745 --> 01:36:40.512
And over the course of this 16 month period,

2663
01:36:40.512 --> 01:36:42.875
like one guy lost 180 pounds or something like that.

2664
01:36:42.875 --> 01:36:43.708
Yeah, yeah.

2665
01:36:43.708 --> 01:36:44.574
Adam, Adam.

2666
01:36:44.574 --> 01:36:46.999
I mean, it's so schmaltzy that it's like,

2667
01:36:46.999 --> 01:36:48.796
oh, what is this a Disney movie?

2668
01:36:48.796 --> 01:36:49.987
This is the guy

2669
01:36:49.987 --> 01:36:53.904
you could see the montage sequence in the movie

2670
01:36:54.819 --> 01:36:56.174
about how that all transpires,

2671
01:36:56.174 --> 01:36:58.345
but there's real beauty in that.

2672
01:36:58.345 --> 01:36:59.672
Well, some good guys too.

2673
01:36:59.672 --> 01:37:03.262
I mean that again, through whatever circumstance,

2674
01:37:03.262 --> 01:37:04.789
I mean, some of them are just addicts.

2675
01:37:04.789 --> 01:37:09.789
Some of 'em had other issues or just bad luck or whatever.

2676
01:37:10.441 --> 01:37:12.495
And there are a few genuine bad guys, of course.

2677
01:37:12.495 --> 01:37:15.181
I mean, prison isn't full of people that,

2678
01:37:15.181 --> 01:37:16.079
that shouldn't be there.

2679
01:37:16.079 --> 01:37:16.912
Right.

2680
01:37:16.912 --> 01:37:17.776
There's a few that should,

2681
01:37:17.776 --> 01:37:21.405
but generally speaking, they were just regular guys.

2682
01:37:21.405 --> 01:37:24.119
And what I found funny is nobody ever,

2683
01:37:24.119 --> 01:37:26.656
of course, came up to me.

2684
01:37:26.656 --> 01:37:29.830
Initially guys even made fun of me to a certain degree,

2685
01:37:29.830 --> 01:37:31.745
which is not unusual for me,

2686
01:37:31.745 --> 01:37:36.291
but through time and the fact that they saw me

2687
01:37:36.291 --> 01:37:38.201
continuing to run and to do these things,

2688
01:37:38.201 --> 01:37:42.204
they would never like approach me in the middle of,

2689
01:37:42.204 --> 01:37:44.216
the cha line or something like that.

2690
01:37:44.216 --> 01:37:46.777
They would come up to me sort of surreptitiously and say,

2691
01:37:46.777 --> 01:37:47.778
Hey-
Yeah, Yeah.

2692
01:37:47.778 --> 01:37:48.877
Man, I'm thinking about,

2693
01:37:48.877 --> 01:37:51.714
I've been thinking about running, you know,

2694
01:37:51.714 --> 01:37:53.312
what do you think I should do?

2695
01:37:53.312 --> 01:37:55.089
Like very quietly.

2696
01:37:55.089 --> 01:37:57.105
I even had a couple of the guards in there,

2697
01:37:57.105 --> 01:37:59.478
who came to me for running advice,

2698
01:37:59.478 --> 01:38:02.744
and that was totally against, you know, any-

2699
01:38:02.744 --> 01:38:03.735
They're not really allowed.

2700
01:38:03.735 --> 01:38:05.074
Any policy, no, no.

2701
01:38:05.074 --> 01:38:08.110
And they were, again, and those guys,

2702
01:38:08.110 --> 01:38:10.951
were, you know, some of them weren't good guys.

2703
01:38:10.951 --> 01:38:12.591
I mean, unfortunately, you take guys

2704
01:38:12.591 --> 01:38:15.217
and give 'em some power in a situation like that,

2705
01:38:15.217 --> 01:38:18.871
and there were a lot that really treated people poorly,

2706
01:38:18.871 --> 01:38:21.497
but there were also plenty who were

2707
01:38:21.497 --> 01:38:24.031
were in fact just doing their job,

2708
01:38:24.031 --> 01:38:26.426
and I never held that against them,

2709
01:38:26.426 --> 01:38:27.932
and were good guys.

2710
01:38:27.932 --> 01:38:30.192
And if they asked me,

2711
01:38:30.192 --> 01:38:31.674
how to start a running program,

2712
01:38:31.674 --> 01:38:36.091
I'd tell an officer just as much as I tell an inmate,

2713
01:38:37.878 --> 01:38:39.111
because running is running.

2714
01:38:39.111 --> 01:38:41.434
If you're willing to,

2715
01:38:41.434 --> 01:38:42.957
if you're willing to take a shot at it,

2716
01:38:42.957 --> 01:38:44.813
then I don't want to ever discourage anybody

2717
01:38:44.813 --> 01:38:49.813
from getting out there and finding what they can do.

2718
01:38:49.902 --> 01:38:50.872
And are you still,

2719
01:38:50.872 --> 01:38:52.574
are you in touch with these guys still?

2720
01:38:52.574 --> 01:38:54.892
You know, that's the irony.

2721
01:38:54.892 --> 01:38:57.110
No, is the answer,

2722
01:38:57.110 --> 01:38:58.865
and the reason is not because I don't wanna be,

2723
01:38:58.865 --> 01:39:01.249
but it's not allowed.

2724
01:39:01.249 --> 01:39:02.790
Oh, former inmate-

2725
01:39:02.790 --> 01:39:03.623
Yeah.

2726
01:39:03.623 --> 01:39:05.274
Can't correspond with somebody who's inside?

2727
01:39:05.274 --> 01:39:06.107
Correct.

2728
01:39:06.107 --> 01:39:06.940
I didn't know that.

2729
01:39:06.940 --> 01:39:07.773
Yeah.

2730
01:39:07.773 --> 01:39:08.676
And actually, technically, I can't,

2731
01:39:08.676 --> 01:39:11.058
I mean, it's been interesting for me just

2732
01:39:11.058 --> 01:39:13.058
because I'm easy to find

2733
01:39:14.403 --> 01:39:16.403
out here in the world.

2734
01:39:16.403 --> 01:39:18.540
And so if somebody that I was in there with

2735
01:39:18.540 --> 01:39:20.448
wants to find me

2736
01:39:20.448 --> 01:39:22.993
through whatever social media or anything else.

2737
01:39:22.993 --> 01:39:23.826
Right.

2738
01:39:23.826 --> 01:39:28.264
It's pretty much impossible to stop,

2739
01:39:28.264 --> 01:39:30.166
although I do laugh every once in a while,

2740
01:39:30.166 --> 01:39:31.790
I get some kind of note from somebody

2741
01:39:31.790 --> 01:39:33.006
and I'll tell you the truth,

2742
01:39:33.006 --> 01:39:34.441
it'll be their real name.

2743
01:39:34.441 --> 01:39:35.674
And I've no idea who it is

2744
01:39:35.674 --> 01:39:36.578
because they've got a name,

2745
01:39:36.578 --> 01:39:37.596
like a ball game.

2746
01:39:37.596 --> 01:39:38.467
It's not by the ball.

2747
01:39:38.467 --> 01:39:39.300
(Charlie laughing)

2748
01:39:39.300 --> 01:39:41.255
Right, but it's interesting.

2749
01:39:41.255 --> 01:39:42.841
It's not allowed, so it's been,

2750
01:39:42.841 --> 01:39:45.017
it's weird and frustrating.

2751
01:39:45.017 --> 01:39:46.263
It'd be like going to college

2752
01:39:46.263 --> 01:39:49.327
for years with guys or being in a fraternity

2753
01:39:49.327 --> 01:39:51.339
or being on some team sometime.

2754
01:39:51.339 --> 01:39:52.513
And then when that's over,

2755
01:39:52.513 --> 01:39:56.846
never being allowed to have contact with them again.

2756
01:39:57.821 --> 01:39:58.963
I don't know, I mean, I assume.

2757
01:39:58.963 --> 01:40:00.124
Can you go visit or no?

2758
01:40:00.124 --> 01:40:01.392
No, God, they won't you visit.

2759
01:40:01.392 --> 01:40:04.186
No, I can't visit, I can't vote, I can't-

2760
01:40:04.186 --> 01:40:06.135
Is the rationale is that you're,

2761
01:40:06.135 --> 01:40:09.100
you could be some sort of proxy for them to

2762
01:40:09.100 --> 01:40:10.891
take care of business in the outside world on their-

2763
01:40:10.891 --> 01:40:11.724
Yeah.
Behalf or something.

2764
01:40:11.724 --> 01:40:12.557
Yeah, not only that,

2765
01:40:12.557 --> 01:40:13.400
it's just that technically,

2766
01:40:13.400 --> 01:40:17.537
if you have supposedly bad guys that are all

2767
01:40:17.537 --> 01:40:19.581
continuing to have contact with each other.

2768
01:40:19.581 --> 01:40:20.414
Right.

2769
01:40:20.414 --> 01:40:22.249
Then that could somehow lead to something.

2770
01:40:22.249 --> 01:40:23.310
I mean, the here,
(Rich laughing)

2771
01:40:23.310 --> 01:40:26.282
the irony I've always found in that is that,

2772
01:40:26.282 --> 01:40:29.565
prison is essentially criminal college.

2773
01:40:29.565 --> 01:40:32.970
I mean, I don't wanna say what I could do

2774
01:40:32.970 --> 01:40:34.367
because I probably get myself in trouble,

2775
01:40:34.367 --> 01:40:38.865
but the stories you hear and the things that you learn-

2776
01:40:38.865 --> 01:40:39.698
You learn some skills.

2777
01:40:39.698 --> 01:40:40.738
You learn how to do.

2778
01:40:40.738 --> 01:40:41.571
You're got some skills.

2779
01:40:41.571 --> 01:40:44.049
(Rich laughing)
I mean, you know,

2780
01:40:44.049 --> 01:40:47.308
my drug past is gonna be right where it belongs

2781
01:40:47.308 --> 01:40:48.926
and that's in the past forever,

2782
01:40:48.926 --> 01:40:51.913
but you know, the ways people do things,

2783
01:40:51.913 --> 01:40:53.567
I mean, and I will say that,

2784
01:40:53.567 --> 01:40:55.932
meth is the killer of today,

2785
01:40:55.932 --> 01:40:59.190
very much like other drugs have been in the past,

2786
01:40:59.190 --> 01:41:01.878
but it's the scourge of the earth right now.

2787
01:41:01.878 --> 01:41:03.831
And you can make it in a bathtub.

2788
01:41:03.831 --> 01:41:07.396
And so it's bad news, but I mean,

2789
01:41:07.396 --> 01:41:10.153
I guess the idea is that they don't want guys

2790
01:41:10.153 --> 01:41:12.951
being able to get together when they get outta prison.

2791
01:41:12.951 --> 01:41:13.810
And there's, you know,

2792
01:41:13.810 --> 01:41:15.940
there is some logic to that,

2793
01:41:15.940 --> 01:41:18.750
but once you've shoved them together

2794
01:41:18.750 --> 01:41:20.737
to basically share information

2795
01:41:20.737 --> 01:41:24.654
in tight quarters for months or years together,

2796
01:41:26.175 --> 01:41:27.474
that ship is kind of sailed.

2797
01:41:27.474 --> 01:41:28.327
Right.

2798
01:41:28.327 --> 01:41:29.783
But so it's frustrating though.

2799
01:41:29.783 --> 01:41:30.616
I mean, I got,

2800
01:41:30.616 --> 01:41:35.038
these guys who were my friends, are my friends.

2801
01:41:35.038 --> 01:41:36.178
They'll always be my friends.

2802
01:41:36.178 --> 01:41:37.197
I mean-
Right.

2803
01:41:37.197 --> 01:41:38.460
From that time.

2804
01:41:38.460 --> 01:41:40.619
I don't have any idea what's happened to any of them

2805
01:41:40.619 --> 01:41:42.202
at this point.

2806
01:41:42.202 --> 01:41:45.115
And so we kind of glossed over the fact

2807
01:41:45.115 --> 01:41:48.301
that you actually ran your version of Badwater

2808
01:41:48.301 --> 01:41:49.593
when you were in prison.

2809
01:41:49.593 --> 01:41:51.730
You had to do it over a couple days, right?

2810
01:41:51.730 --> 01:41:52.708
I did.

2811
01:41:52.708 --> 01:41:53.999
'Cause they really let you run

2812
01:41:53.999 --> 01:41:54.832
a couple hours a day.

2813
01:41:54.832 --> 01:41:56.740
Yeah, well, they discourage,

2814
01:41:56.740 --> 01:41:58.540
I think the rules probably even say,

2815
01:41:58.540 --> 01:41:59.815
you're not supposed to run more than

2816
01:41:59.815 --> 01:42:03.014
three miles at any time or something and-

2817
01:42:03.014 --> 01:42:04.551
They made an exception for you.

2818
01:42:04.551 --> 01:42:05.932
Well, they, you know,

2819
01:42:05.932 --> 01:42:07.049
they didn't really make an exception.

2820
01:42:07.049 --> 01:42:07.949
I just sort of did it,

2821
01:42:07.949 --> 01:42:11.782
but it is, I still had to go inside for count.

2822
01:42:14.872 --> 01:42:17.570
And obviously, I had to sleep inside.

2823
01:42:17.570 --> 01:42:19.742
But they let you go out in the yard all day

2824
01:42:19.742 --> 01:42:20.575
and do it?

2825
01:42:20.575 --> 01:42:21.408
Camps, yeah.

2826
01:42:21.408 --> 01:42:24.169
A camp is interesting because you do have,

2827
01:42:24.169 --> 01:42:25.268
you have jobs.

2828
01:42:25.268 --> 01:42:27.052
I mean, my job working in recreation.

2829
01:42:27.052 --> 01:42:29.822
And so I had to like clean the pool tables every morning

2830
01:42:29.822 --> 01:42:32.989
and there's some, I had specific jobs,

2831
01:42:34.543 --> 01:42:36.707
and then I taught classes.

2832
01:42:36.707 --> 01:42:39.594
The addiction recovery classes, those kinds of things.

2833
01:42:39.594 --> 01:42:41.677
But in a sense at a camp,

2834
01:42:42.830 --> 01:42:44.219
there is, you know,

2835
01:42:44.219 --> 01:42:46.467
there's guys in there that have to work.

2836
01:42:46.467 --> 01:42:48.467
I was lucky enough that,

2837
01:42:50.322 --> 01:42:52.959
I had some support, it was my own money,

2838
01:42:52.959 --> 01:42:53.792
but I had some,

2839
01:42:53.792 --> 01:42:56.985
I had the ability to get some money every month.

2840
01:42:56.985 --> 01:42:58.708
And then, I mean, there's a limit to that.

2841
01:42:58.708 --> 01:42:59.711
It's very complicated.

2842
01:42:59.711 --> 01:43:03.336
But suffice it to say some guys in there,

2843
01:43:03.336 --> 01:43:04.286
there's nobody that,

2844
01:43:04.286 --> 01:43:05.391
they don't have anybody on the outside.

2845
01:43:05.391 --> 01:43:06.224
Right.

2846
01:43:06.224 --> 01:43:09.412
If they don't earn $10 or a $100

2847
01:43:09.412 --> 01:43:11.983
or whatever it might be that month,

2848
01:43:11.983 --> 01:43:16.288
then they can't go buy a new pair of tennis shoes-

2849
01:43:16.288 --> 01:43:17.121
Right.

2850
01:43:17.121 --> 01:43:17.954
At the commissary,

2851
01:43:17.954 --> 01:43:21.423
or they can't get snacks or coffee or anything else.

2852
01:43:21.423 --> 01:43:23.724
And so those guys work.

2853
01:43:23.724 --> 01:43:24.557
Right.

2854
01:43:24.557 --> 01:43:26.102
And very often what you'll see,

2855
01:43:26.102 --> 01:43:28.071
not to be too detailed, but where you see a camp,

2856
01:43:28.071 --> 01:43:30.656
you'll usually see like a medium present,

2857
01:43:30.656 --> 01:43:31.864
a higher level security.

2858
01:43:31.864 --> 01:43:33.548
And it's really a lot of the guys at the camp,

2859
01:43:33.548 --> 01:43:37.659
it's their job to actually take care of the grounds

2860
01:43:37.659 --> 01:43:39.277
or whatever it might be

2861
01:43:39.277 --> 01:43:42.063
for the higher level security presence.

2862
01:43:42.063 --> 01:43:47.063
So it's a very intricate, interesting, weird twisted system.

2863
01:43:48.916 --> 01:43:52.083
For me, I was able to teach my classes

2864
01:43:53.094 --> 01:43:56.382
and to do those things in a way that allowed me,

2865
01:43:56.382 --> 01:43:57.262
a lot of freedom during the day.

2866
01:43:57.262 --> 01:43:58.095
Get quite the money there.

2867
01:43:58.095 --> 01:43:58.928
Yeah.

2868
01:43:58.928 --> 01:44:00.296
And so, I mean, I could go,

2869
01:44:00.296 --> 01:44:01.418
I could go run so-

2870
01:44:01.418 --> 01:44:03.262
You're just running around a yard,

2871
01:44:03.262 --> 01:44:04.095
that's what?

2872
01:44:04.095 --> 01:44:05.056
Like a quarter mile in perimeter-

2873
01:44:05.056 --> 01:44:05.914
Yeah,
Or whatever.

2874
01:44:05.914 --> 01:44:08.321
I call it a goat path 'cause it even had a hill.

2875
01:44:08.321 --> 01:44:11.612
So I had to decide, did I want to run

2876
01:44:11.612 --> 01:44:16.612
the direction that meant that I went up a sharp steeper hill

2877
01:44:17.127 --> 01:44:19.360
on one way or the other direction had a much-

2878
01:44:19.360 --> 01:44:21.722
Yeah, you had that short, steep down,

2879
01:44:21.722 --> 01:44:25.356
but you had a much longer gradual up, I don't know.

2880
01:44:25.356 --> 01:44:27.722
It was very, like any runner I overthought of-

2881
01:44:27.722 --> 01:44:29.738
I was laying in bed at night,

2882
01:44:29.738 --> 01:44:31.196
like pondering this deep-

2883
01:44:31.196 --> 01:44:32.029
I should go that way.

2884
01:44:32.029 --> 01:44:33.695
Decision that you have to make.

2885
01:44:33.695 --> 01:44:34.528
Is that way faster?

2886
01:44:34.528 --> 01:44:35.361
(Rich laughing)
Is the other way faster?

2887
01:44:35.361 --> 01:44:37.715
But, you know, I got to where I was doing.

2888
01:44:37.715 --> 01:44:39.099
I mean, I did speed work.

2889
01:44:39.099 --> 01:44:40.452
I did all kinds of stuff in there.

2890
01:44:40.452 --> 01:44:42.491
And even was able to,

2891
01:44:42.491 --> 01:44:44.604
I ran a few five minute miles in there

2892
01:44:44.604 --> 01:44:47.858
and did some things I hadn't done for many, many years.

2893
01:44:47.858 --> 01:44:50.949
So just because I had the time to do it.

2894
01:44:50.949 --> 01:44:52.519
And you know, I read.

2895
01:44:52.519 --> 01:44:53.716
Yeah, you're not gonna be a return

2896
01:44:53.716 --> 01:44:54.694
any phone calls or anything?

2897
01:44:54.694 --> 01:44:55.527
No.

2898
01:44:55.527 --> 01:44:59.316
I read 150 books, I wrote every day.

2899
01:44:59.316 --> 01:45:02.358
I did my best under really stressful circumstances

2900
01:45:02.358 --> 01:45:06.025
to take care of my body, but also my spirit,

2901
01:45:07.073 --> 01:45:11.049
and that was done by helping other people.

2902
01:45:11.049 --> 01:45:14.303
And look, you know, from being in recovery,

2903
01:45:14.303 --> 01:45:16.025
talk about helping other people,

2904
01:45:16.025 --> 01:45:18.757
sounds very giving and very generous.

2905
01:45:18.757 --> 01:45:21.983
And we know in addiction recovery

2906
01:45:21.983 --> 01:45:23.686
that the thing that I can do that is,

2907
01:45:23.686 --> 01:45:26.091
is absolutely the most selfish thing I can do

2908
01:45:26.091 --> 01:45:27.941
and best for me is to help someone else.

2909
01:45:27.941 --> 01:45:28.839
Right.

2910
01:45:28.839 --> 01:45:31.648
And so I set my sights on,

2911
01:45:31.648 --> 01:45:35.061
on doing that and still, hopefully still do.

2912
01:45:35.061 --> 01:45:39.228
I get a lot of requests to speak and to do things,

2913
01:45:40.324 --> 01:45:42.968
talk to kids and adults alike.

2914
01:45:42.968 --> 01:45:45.401
And I try to never say no to those things

2915
01:45:45.401 --> 01:45:48.384
just because I think it's what I'm required to do.

2916
01:45:48.384 --> 01:45:50.099
Yeah, if you wanna,

2917
01:45:50.099 --> 01:45:51.015
if you wanna keep it-
Yeah.

2918
01:45:51.015 --> 01:45:51.848
You gotta give it away.

2919
01:45:51.848 --> 01:45:52.681
Exactly.

2920
01:45:52.681 --> 01:45:54.296
So how did the Twitter thing work?

2921
01:45:54.296 --> 01:45:55.129
You gotta answer this.

2922
01:45:55.129 --> 01:45:55.991
Drive me crazy.

2923
01:45:55.991 --> 01:45:58.408
Yeah, so I had a,

2924
01:45:59.903 --> 01:46:02.664
the way prisons work these days is they do federal prisons

2925
01:46:02.664 --> 01:46:05.487
are equipped with computers these days.

2926
01:46:05.487 --> 01:46:07.815
It's very expensive and it's very limited,

2927
01:46:07.815 --> 01:46:10.174
the amount of time you can spend on it.

2928
01:46:10.174 --> 01:46:11.215
So what I would do is

2929
01:46:11.215 --> 01:46:14.798
I would actually write my tweets in advance

2930
01:46:16.193 --> 01:46:19.644
and sometimes I would mail them out in a letter.

2931
01:46:19.644 --> 01:46:21.364
Sometimes I would get on email,

2932
01:46:21.364 --> 01:46:24.524
but that was heavily, that was monitored by,

2933
01:46:24.524 --> 01:46:25.357
by the system.

2934
01:46:25.357 --> 01:46:26.190
But it wasn't illegal.

2935
01:46:26.190 --> 01:46:27.866
It's not, you know, again,

2936
01:46:27.866 --> 01:46:29.334
it did turn into a,

2937
01:46:29.334 --> 01:46:30.480
they didn't care for it.

2938
01:46:30.480 --> 01:46:31.528
Let's just put it that way.

2939
01:46:31.528 --> 01:46:32.488
They weren't happy about the fact

2940
01:46:32.488 --> 01:46:33.779
that you're tweeting from.

2941
01:46:33.779 --> 01:46:35.240
No, they weren't happy about it.

2942
01:46:35.240 --> 01:46:36.679
But the fact of the matter is,

2943
01:46:36.679 --> 01:46:38.501
and someone else had to actually-

2944
01:46:38.501 --> 01:46:40.083
Type the tweet.
Exactly.

2945
01:46:40.083 --> 01:46:41.348
Right?
Exactly.

2946
01:46:41.348 --> 01:46:43.503
But that happens every day,

2947
01:46:43.503 --> 01:46:45.965
all over the place and it's not illegal,

2948
01:46:45.965 --> 01:46:48.162
and I wasn't, you know,

2949
01:46:48.162 --> 01:46:50.169
if I had been sending out posts that said,

2950
01:46:50.169 --> 01:46:51.851
here's how you sneak some contraband into me.

2951
01:46:51.851 --> 01:46:53.259
Yeah.

2952
01:46:53.259 --> 01:46:55.923
Or naming the guard by his name and-

2953
01:46:55.923 --> 01:46:57.589
Or yeah, anything
(Rich laughing)

2954
01:46:57.589 --> 01:46:59.482
or even an inmate by his name,

2955
01:46:59.482 --> 01:47:01.342
then that's not cool.

2956
01:47:01.342 --> 01:47:02.778
I wouldn't have done that.

2957
01:47:02.778 --> 01:47:04.698
But it was all generic.

2958
01:47:04.698 --> 01:47:06.968
I mean, my favorite one was I did

2959
01:47:06.968 --> 01:47:10.278
this whole little series called Overheard.

2960
01:47:10.278 --> 01:47:11.111
I remember that.

2961
01:47:11.111 --> 01:47:11.944
Yeah.

2962
01:47:11.944 --> 01:47:12.777
And there was some,

2963
01:47:12.777 --> 01:47:13.800
there was some funny stuff,

2964
01:47:13.800 --> 01:47:16.967
because guys in there, would just say,

2965
01:47:19.082 --> 01:47:21.506
say some crazy things.

2966
01:47:21.506 --> 01:47:23.466
I don't even know if I can give an example.

2967
01:47:23.466 --> 01:47:24.420
And I'm trying to remember.

2968
01:47:24.420 --> 01:47:26.688
Well, I'm standing in line for lunch one day.

2969
01:47:26.688 --> 01:47:28.577
And these two guys are talking in front of me,

2970
01:47:28.577 --> 01:47:30.635
and one of 'em looks at the other one and says,

2971
01:47:30.635 --> 01:47:32.085
now, wait a minute.

2972
01:47:32.085 --> 01:47:35.800
Exactly what part of the cow does the liver come from?

2973
01:47:35.800 --> 01:47:37.047
(Rich laughing)

2974
01:47:37.047 --> 01:47:39.865
Because like we were having liver and onions that day.

2975
01:47:39.865 --> 01:47:41.198
And another guy asked me,

2976
01:47:41.198 --> 01:47:43.161
he asked me, he is like, now, you know,

2977
01:47:43.161 --> 01:47:46.650
how many laps around this track equals a cupcake?

2978
01:47:46.650 --> 01:47:47.599
Right.

2979
01:47:47.599 --> 01:47:48.501
Things like that.

2980
01:47:48.501 --> 01:47:49.913
And I mean, they're just,

2981
01:47:49.913 --> 01:47:53.749
they're great, funny, genuine questions and some,

2982
01:47:53.749 --> 01:47:57.020
and also some heart wrenching things,

2983
01:47:57.020 --> 01:47:58.868
guys who-
I have no doubt.

2984
01:47:58.868 --> 01:48:00.765
Who hadn't seen their kids for 10 years

2985
01:48:00.765 --> 01:48:05.663
and they're getting to visit that day and things like that.

2986
01:48:05.663 --> 01:48:06.629
I mean speaking of that,

2987
01:48:06.629 --> 01:48:09.134
how has that kind of colored your relationship

2988
01:48:09.134 --> 01:48:10.285
with your sons?

2989
01:48:10.285 --> 01:48:11.974
I mean, how has that?
Man.

2990
01:48:11.974 --> 01:48:13.036
How's that impacted?

2991
01:48:13.036 --> 01:48:14.115
Well, my kids are doing great,

2992
01:48:14.115 --> 01:48:15.195
but I couldn't have,

2993
01:48:15.195 --> 01:48:17.454
I couldn't have been taken away from them.

2994
01:48:17.454 --> 01:48:19.417
I mean, is there ever a good time,

2995
01:48:19.417 --> 01:48:22.834
but they were teenage boys and, you know,

2996
01:48:23.984 --> 01:48:26.705
one of them, my youngest is now a freshman

2997
01:48:26.705 --> 01:48:28.481
at UNC in Chapel Hill

2998
01:48:28.481 --> 01:48:32.326
and he's, you know, to say they survived it

2999
01:48:32.326 --> 01:48:34.638
and got through it okay,

3000
01:48:34.638 --> 01:48:37.745
is just to acknowledge the physical manifestation

3001
01:48:37.745 --> 01:48:38.693
of what happened.

3002
01:48:38.693 --> 01:48:40.080
I mean, you know, they're still alive.

3003
01:48:40.080 --> 01:48:40.913
They're alive.

3004
01:48:40.913 --> 01:48:42.132
They're doing their thing,

3005
01:48:42.132 --> 01:48:43.382
they're living their lives,

3006
01:48:43.382 --> 01:48:45.799
but it's a pretty scary thing

3007
01:48:47.769 --> 01:48:51.936
for teenage boy to just have their dad taken away.

3008
01:48:53.385 --> 01:48:56.526
And my older sons had some addiction issues himself

3009
01:48:56.526 --> 01:48:59.693
and he's doing fantastically right now

3010
01:49:01.123 --> 01:49:02.577
and he's a personal trainer

3011
01:49:02.577 --> 01:49:05.498
and I'm hoping that both of them get to come out

3012
01:49:05.498 --> 01:49:08.314
during Run2Boston and spend some time out on the road

3013
01:49:08.314 --> 01:49:10.564
and to helping out.

3014
01:49:10.564 --> 01:49:12.305
You know, they're doing well,

3015
01:49:12.305 --> 01:49:15.722
but it, you know, it destroyed my family,

3016
01:49:16.622 --> 01:49:19.039
and the shock waves from that

3017
01:49:20.077 --> 01:49:23.437
will probably never go away fully.

3018
01:49:23.437 --> 01:49:26.909
But I say to them the same thing that I'd say to anybody,

3019
01:49:26.909 --> 01:49:29.709
nobody can ruin my life, except for me.

3020
01:49:29.709 --> 01:49:31.032
(Charlie laughing)

3021
01:49:31.032 --> 01:49:33.782
Nobody gets the right to do that.

3022
01:49:34.803 --> 01:49:36.794
Not some federal agent,

3023
01:49:36.794 --> 01:49:40.593
not prison, not a prison guard, not anybody.

3024
01:49:40.593 --> 01:49:42.776
I'm fully capable of messing up my own life.

3025
01:49:42.776 --> 01:49:44.395
Right.

3026
01:49:44.395 --> 01:49:46.416
But to kind of come out of Beckley

3027
01:49:46.416 --> 01:49:49.369
and carry that pain of knowing that,

3028
01:49:49.369 --> 01:49:51.890
what happened really impacted those boys.

3029
01:49:51.890 --> 01:49:52.723
Yeah.

3030
01:49:52.723 --> 01:49:54.117
You know, in a profound way.

3031
01:49:54.117 --> 01:49:56.863
And how do you kind of move forward with that?

3032
01:49:56.863 --> 01:49:58.921
Well, and as a father, they, you know,

3033
01:49:58.921 --> 01:50:00.592
I called them and I wrote,

3034
01:50:00.592 --> 01:50:02.249
and I would do all the things that I could.

3035
01:50:02.249 --> 01:50:03.646
And it was, at the beginning,

3036
01:50:03.646 --> 01:50:07.813
we had a lot of contact and as time moved forward,

3037
01:50:08.980 --> 01:50:12.886
what I was, and this is my kids are loving boys

3038
01:50:12.886 --> 01:50:16.580
who both will hug and kiss me in public.

3039
01:50:16.580 --> 01:50:17.413
Right.

3040
01:50:17.413 --> 01:50:20.055
And I judged that as success as a father,

3041
01:50:20.055 --> 01:50:23.006
but they to protect themselves actually,

3042
01:50:23.006 --> 01:50:25.884
had to like withdraw from me to a certain degree.

3043
01:50:25.884 --> 01:50:28.492
I mean, it was almost like too painful to hear from me.

3044
01:50:28.492 --> 01:50:29.352
Right.

3045
01:50:29.352 --> 01:50:31.540
And I tried to respect that

3046
01:50:31.540 --> 01:50:33.368
and to not try to be,

3047
01:50:33.368 --> 01:50:35.966
and one of the hardest things to do is to try to

3048
01:50:35.966 --> 01:50:40.170
stay in touch, but also try to not be like a parent.

3049
01:50:40.170 --> 01:50:42.472
Like I couldn't tell them what to do-

3050
01:50:42.472 --> 01:50:43.305
Right.

3051
01:50:43.305 --> 01:50:45.806
From the situation I was in.

3052
01:50:45.806 --> 01:50:47.221
And, you know, again,

3053
01:50:47.221 --> 01:50:49.613
and I watched other guys, I learned from other guys,

3054
01:50:49.613 --> 01:50:53.931
I had a guy, black, who was listed on your list there.

3055
01:50:53.931 --> 01:50:55.872
And he had a son,

3056
01:50:55.872 --> 01:50:58.084
who was one of the top basketball players in the country.

3057
01:50:58.084 --> 01:51:00.497
And he's the first one who said to me,

3058
01:51:00.497 --> 01:51:02.218
"Man, you gotta let it go.

3059
01:51:02.218 --> 01:51:03.598
You gotta let it go."

3060
01:51:03.598 --> 01:51:05.938
'Cause I'd call, and I wouldn't hear back.

3061
01:51:05.938 --> 01:51:08.831
I'd go weeks sometimes without hearing from my own kids.

3062
01:51:08.831 --> 01:51:10.233
And he'd say, "You gotta let it go.

3063
01:51:10.233 --> 01:51:12.882
They're in their own pain right now,

3064
01:51:12.882 --> 01:51:15.516
and you just gotta let 'em get through it.

3065
01:51:15.516 --> 01:51:19.169
You can't save them and they can't save you.

3066
01:51:19.169 --> 01:51:21.615
Do your time, don't let your time do you."

3067
01:51:21.615 --> 01:51:23.173
Right, right.

3068
01:51:23.173 --> 01:51:26.256
And there's this incredible dichotomy

3069
01:51:27.699 --> 01:51:31.616
between your Beckley, which equals imprisonment

3070
01:51:33.061 --> 01:51:36.571
and running, which is ultimate freedom, right?

3071
01:51:36.571 --> 01:51:39.269
These two worlds butting up against each other

3072
01:51:39.269 --> 01:51:42.914
and your ability to find freedom through running

3073
01:51:42.914 --> 01:51:44.298
during your imprisonment.

3074
01:51:44.298 --> 01:51:48.564
It's kind of like this Venn diagram kind of situation.

3075
01:51:48.564 --> 01:51:50.236
And I was thinking about that last night

3076
01:51:50.236 --> 01:51:51.266
when I was going to bed,

3077
01:51:51.266 --> 01:51:56.230
like the two extremes butting up against each other

3078
01:51:56.230 --> 01:52:00.716
and somebody who's used to experiencing that kind of freedom

3079
01:52:00.716 --> 01:52:02.775
going all the way to the other side.

3080
01:52:02.775 --> 01:52:04.648
Well, and I had had a close friend

3081
01:52:04.648 --> 01:52:06.924
who said to me, before I went to Beckley,

3082
01:52:06.924 --> 01:52:09.003
and he was honest with me.

3083
01:52:09.003 --> 01:52:12.846
He said, you know, I can't imagine anybody less suited

3084
01:52:12.846 --> 01:52:15.838
to lose their freedom than you, because I am,

3085
01:52:15.838 --> 01:52:16.921
and in a way,

3086
01:52:18.171 --> 01:52:20.421
even my conviction in a way

3087
01:52:21.780 --> 01:52:24.152
was an attack of lifestyle,

3088
01:52:24.152 --> 01:52:26.666
because my lifestyle is not normal.

3089
01:52:26.666 --> 01:52:31.406
I don't, you know, I've never worked like nine to five,

3090
01:52:31.406 --> 01:52:34.152
not because I just really have proven myself

3091
01:52:34.152 --> 01:52:37.743
very incapable of being able to do it,

3092
01:52:37.743 --> 01:52:39.328
and so it's really a shortcoming.

3093
01:52:39.328 --> 01:52:40.913
It's not a anything else.

3094
01:52:40.913 --> 01:52:44.373
But I always sacrificed some security and money

3095
01:52:44.373 --> 01:52:47.011
and those things to maintain my freedom.

3096
01:52:47.011 --> 01:52:47.844
Right.

3097
01:52:47.844 --> 01:52:49.233
Because that's what I wanted.

3098
01:52:49.233 --> 01:52:53.588
I wanted to be able to go run or to go travel

3099
01:52:53.588 --> 01:52:56.035
or go to a race or go do those things

3100
01:52:56.035 --> 01:52:57.248
when I wanted to do it.

3101
01:52:57.248 --> 01:52:58.973
And that was more important to me

3102
01:52:58.973 --> 01:53:02.185
than having money in the bank and-

3103
01:53:02.185 --> 01:53:03.680
So the irony
(Charlie laughing)

3104
01:53:03.680 --> 01:53:05.677
is all the more palpable.

3105
01:53:05.677 --> 01:53:07.281
Yeah, and I look at, you know what?

3106
01:53:07.281 --> 01:53:10.696
It's the same reason that just a couple of days I got up

3107
01:53:10.696 --> 01:53:14.267
at five o'clock in the morning to go run

3108
01:53:14.267 --> 01:53:18.823
around a track in North Carolina for 10 hours in training

3109
01:53:18.823 --> 01:53:22.017
and working on my pacing, as I was saying.

3110
01:53:22.017 --> 01:53:24.350
I did that because I want to

3111
01:53:25.417 --> 01:53:27.906
prove to myself, not to anybody else,

3112
01:53:27.906 --> 01:53:31.402
but that I can do the things that are are difficult

3113
01:53:31.402 --> 01:53:33.497
and that I don't want to do.

3114
01:53:33.497 --> 01:53:36.603
And that I know I'll be stronger if I can do it.

3115
01:53:36.603 --> 01:53:38.812
And prison forced me to face that,

3116
01:53:38.812 --> 01:53:40.954
a thousand times over.

3117
01:53:40.954 --> 01:53:42.691
Well, yeah, and it's a way of sort of

3118
01:53:42.691 --> 01:53:44.546
staying connected to that experience, right?

3119
01:53:44.546 --> 01:53:46.405
It's sort of like the,

3120
01:53:46.405 --> 01:53:48.484
the homeless guy who's given a bed

3121
01:53:48.484 --> 01:53:49.807
and still sleeps on the floor.

3122
01:53:49.807 --> 01:53:50.724
Yeah.

3123
01:53:50.724 --> 01:53:52.748
Yeah, you almost don't want to get too comfortable.

3124
01:53:52.748 --> 01:53:55.757
And I will say it and you know, I don't,

3125
01:53:55.757 --> 01:53:57.446
I ever like to be a fear monger,

3126
01:53:57.446 --> 01:54:00.634
but I never imagined something like that

3127
01:54:00.634 --> 01:54:02.777
could have ever happened to me.

3128
01:54:02.777 --> 01:54:05.202
And most people can't,

3129
01:54:05.202 --> 01:54:07.620
most people don't go through their lives thinking,

3130
01:54:07.620 --> 01:54:11.068
oh man, at any time I could be arrested and go to prison.

3131
01:54:11.068 --> 01:54:12.247
(Rich laughing)
(Charlie laughing)

3132
01:54:12.247 --> 01:54:13.080
And yet,

3133
01:54:15.738 --> 01:54:17.289
and not to get off on another big tangent,

3134
01:54:17.289 --> 01:54:20.232
you look at all the stuff going on with Edward Snowden

3135
01:54:20.232 --> 01:54:25.232
and just the, you know, all the things being disclosed now.

3136
01:54:25.406 --> 01:54:28.654
It's an interesting place we live in these days

3137
01:54:28.654 --> 01:54:30.994
where there's very little privacy.

3138
01:54:30.994 --> 01:54:33.947
There's very little, that's not suspect,

3139
01:54:33.947 --> 01:54:38.162
and somehow we've become afraid of our own shadows,

3140
01:54:38.162 --> 01:54:41.083
and that somehow justifies that,

3141
01:54:41.083 --> 01:54:44.035
that nothing should be private any longer.

3142
01:54:44.035 --> 01:54:45.981
It's a very bizarre mashup,

3143
01:54:45.981 --> 01:54:47.177
because on the one hand,

3144
01:54:47.177 --> 01:54:50.182
we've never had more access to more information.

3145
01:54:50.182 --> 01:54:52.715
So there's a level of transparency that

3146
01:54:52.715 --> 01:54:56.080
you would think would translate into

3147
01:54:56.080 --> 01:54:59.157
sort of greater personal sovereignty, et cetera.

3148
01:54:59.157 --> 01:55:02.261
And yet at the same time we have this clampdown

3149
01:55:02.261 --> 01:55:03.139
kind of happening

3150
01:55:03.139 --> 01:55:05.853
or this consolidation of governmental power

3151
01:55:05.853 --> 01:55:07.865
that we're all kind of signing off on

3152
01:55:07.865 --> 01:55:10.158
willingly kind of volunteering for it.

3153
01:55:10.158 --> 01:55:13.991
And in a very Orwellian kind of sense that we,

3154
01:55:14.954 --> 01:55:17.371
people say, well, the NSA can

3155
01:55:18.241 --> 01:55:20.597
access your iPhone and it can turn on your camera

3156
01:55:20.597 --> 01:55:23.170
and the microphone and listen to you.

3157
01:55:23.170 --> 01:55:25.457
And everyone's like, okay, all right,

3158
01:55:25.457 --> 01:55:27.171
so what are we doing tonight?

3159
01:55:27.171 --> 01:55:30.075
We're just sort of yawning over this whole thing and.

3160
01:55:30.075 --> 01:55:31.077
(Rich laughing)

3161
01:55:31.077 --> 01:55:31.998
I think we feel powerless.

3162
01:55:31.998 --> 01:55:33.983
It's like, well, what am I supposed to do?

3163
01:55:33.983 --> 01:55:36.284
I guess I'll enjoy my day or-

3164
01:55:36.284 --> 01:55:37.472
I'm not gonna give up my iPhone.

3165
01:55:37.472 --> 01:55:38.736
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

3166
01:55:38.736 --> 01:55:39.569
Forget about that.

3167
01:55:39.569 --> 01:55:40.521
(Charlie laughing)
(Rich laughing)

3168
01:55:40.521 --> 01:55:41.354
Well, and it is,

3169
01:55:41.354 --> 01:55:43.225
we laugh about it but it is,

3170
01:55:43.225 --> 01:55:44.494
it's a question that I think.

3171
01:55:44.494 --> 01:55:47.467
I mean, I'm sort of enjoying watching it in the media

3172
01:55:47.467 --> 01:55:49.881
because it's become,

3173
01:55:49.881 --> 01:55:54.473
it's become a really hotly debated topic as it should be,

3174
01:55:54.473 --> 01:55:59.451
and I don't have the answers and I consider myself to be,

3175
01:55:59.451 --> 01:56:02.771
I consider myself to be a true patriot.

3176
01:56:02.771 --> 01:56:03.770
I mean, I am a patriot.

3177
01:56:03.770 --> 01:56:07.404
I certainly believe in all the basis

3178
01:56:07.404 --> 01:56:10.195
of what this country was built on and its freedoms.

3179
01:56:10.195 --> 01:56:13.721
And I think it's very debatable that we even

3180
01:56:13.721 --> 01:56:15.471
resemble any of that,

3181
01:56:16.786 --> 01:56:21.179
vision that our forefathers had these days,

3182
01:56:21.179 --> 01:56:23.184
and some of that is inevitable change

3183
01:56:23.184 --> 01:56:26.643
that's come through growth and technology and in other ways,

3184
01:56:26.643 --> 01:56:29.810
but some of it's a psychological shift

3185
01:56:30.792 --> 01:56:32.902
that we're just comfortable

3186
01:56:32.902 --> 01:56:35.993
and we're just kind of okay with the stuff that,

3187
01:56:35.993 --> 01:56:38.852
that we feel powerless to control.

3188
01:56:38.852 --> 01:56:40.843
And, you know,

3189
01:56:40.843 --> 01:56:42.443
I don't have the answers either-

3190
01:56:42.443 --> 01:56:43.276
I don't either.

3191
01:56:43.276 --> 01:56:44.109
But I know that,

3192
01:56:44.109 --> 01:56:45.757
I know that asking the questions

3193
01:56:45.757 --> 01:56:47.916
and continuing to talk about it is really important.

3194
01:56:47.916 --> 01:56:49.653
I think people are a little fed up

3195
01:56:49.653 --> 01:56:51.153
and worried though

3196
01:56:52.979 --> 01:56:56.053
about where the direction it's all heading.

3197
01:56:56.053 --> 01:56:58.458
And I'm glad we should be worried.

3198
01:56:58.458 --> 01:56:59.846
But we're not

3199
01:56:59.846 --> 01:57:02.700
sort of rallying in the streets like Vietnam era.

3200
01:57:02.700 --> 01:57:03.571
No.

3201
01:57:03.571 --> 01:57:04.404
We're too distracted.

3202
01:57:04.404 --> 01:57:05.237
We're too busy for that.

3203
01:57:05.237 --> 01:57:07.021
We're too, well, we're busy,

3204
01:57:07.021 --> 01:57:08.673
but we're busy doing what?
Yeah.

3205
01:57:08.673 --> 01:57:11.105
We're busy distracting ourselves with

3206
01:57:11.105 --> 01:57:12.612
technology and convenience.

3207
01:57:12.612 --> 01:57:13.566
Yeah, yeah.

3208
01:57:13.566 --> 01:57:15.308
And disposable content.

3209
01:57:15.308 --> 01:57:16.215
And running.

3210
01:57:16.215 --> 01:57:17.067
(Rich laughing)
And running.

3211
01:57:17.067 --> 01:57:18.062
Well, I'll just out running anyway.

3212
01:57:18.062 --> 01:57:19.168
Very good, yeah.
(Charlie laughing)

3213
01:57:19.168 --> 01:57:21.549
No, well, we've been going for almost two hours.

3214
01:57:21.549 --> 01:57:23.556
I don't wanna keep you too much longer, but we do,

3215
01:57:23.556 --> 01:57:25.550
I do wanna say, could sort of,

3216
01:57:25.550 --> 01:57:27.758
in the wake of getting out of Beckley,

3217
01:57:27.758 --> 01:57:32.001
it was a mere year later where you show up at Badwater.

3218
01:57:32.001 --> 01:57:33.362
Right?

3219
01:57:33.362 --> 01:57:36.156
And I mean, what were your expectations

3220
01:57:36.156 --> 01:57:38.608
returning to that race?

3221
01:57:38.608 --> 01:57:40.711
I wanted to be under the radar,

3222
01:57:40.711 --> 01:57:42.822
like as much as I possibly could be,

3223
01:57:42.822 --> 01:57:44.313
which is at that point.

3224
01:57:44.313 --> 01:57:45.755
Which is not being possible.

3225
01:57:45.755 --> 01:57:46.588
Yes.

3226
01:57:46.588 --> 01:57:48.187
Especially at Badwater, I mean.

3227
01:57:48.187 --> 01:57:50.337
But Chris Kostman the race director,

3228
01:57:50.337 --> 01:57:53.812
who I consider a friend and a great guy and-

3229
01:57:53.812 --> 01:57:54.845
He lives down the street here.

3230
01:57:54.845 --> 01:57:55.892
Oh, you saw him right?

3231
01:57:55.892 --> 01:57:57.225
I saw him at the supermarket the other day.

3232
01:57:57.225 --> 01:57:58.482
Yeah, yeah, in the Canyon area.

3233
01:57:58.482 --> 01:58:01.499
And actually, we don't have time to talk about it today,

3234
01:58:01.499 --> 01:58:04.664
but everybody out there should Google Badwater right now.

3235
01:58:04.664 --> 01:58:05.667
Right.

3236
01:58:05.667 --> 01:58:06.500
And then national parks and all that stuff.

3237
01:58:06.500 --> 01:58:08.030
Well, I tweeted, I tweeted about that.

3238
01:58:08.030 --> 01:58:09.351
I mean, I'm sure you saw that article about-

3239
01:58:09.351 --> 01:58:10.684
I did.

3240
01:58:10.684 --> 01:58:12.271
The radiation and that caused-

3241
01:58:12.271 --> 01:58:13.104
Yeah.

3242
01:58:13.104 --> 01:58:13.937
A big reaction with people,

3243
01:58:13.937 --> 01:58:16.977
because it's kind of a suspect story,

3244
01:58:16.977 --> 01:58:20.422
basically there's not gonna be any adventure core racing

3245
01:58:20.422 --> 01:58:21.828
in Death Valley.
Death Valley.

3246
01:58:21.828 --> 01:58:23.017
They have their permits.

3247
01:58:23.017 --> 01:58:23.850
Yeah, yeah.

3248
01:58:23.850 --> 01:58:25.505
We not rubber stamped.

3249
01:58:25.505 --> 01:58:26.840
It's crazy.
The first time.

3250
01:58:26.840 --> 01:58:27.673
It's crazy.

3251
01:58:27.673 --> 01:58:31.817
I mean, the economic impact alone in Death Valley

3252
01:58:31.817 --> 01:58:32.682
is fantastic.

3253
01:58:32.682 --> 01:58:34.319
And the tourism,

3254
01:58:34.319 --> 01:58:37.664
I think that tangentially comes from

3255
01:58:37.664 --> 01:58:39.395
the notoriety that a race like Badwater has.

3256
01:58:39.395 --> 01:58:40.228
Yeah.

3257
01:58:40.228 --> 01:58:41.205
I mean, it brings people

3258
01:58:41.205 --> 01:58:42.038
from all over the world.
Yeah.

3259
01:58:42.038 --> 01:58:43.125
They'd have see this place.

3260
01:58:43.125 --> 01:58:43.958
They have valley.

3261
01:58:43.958 --> 01:58:44.791
Yeah, so it's gonna-

3262
01:58:44.791 --> 01:58:46.820
I mean do you have any behind the scenes

3263
01:58:46.820 --> 01:58:49.772
knowledge about that, that you can impart or not?

3264
01:58:49.772 --> 01:58:50.605
I really don't,

3265
01:58:50.605 --> 01:58:52.018
although that I know that every summer

3266
01:58:52.018 --> 01:58:54.395
there's a lot of Germans around in Death Valley.

3267
01:58:54.395 --> 01:58:55.228
(Charlie laughing)

3268
01:58:55.228 --> 01:58:57.164
It always fascinate me.
What?

3269
01:58:57.164 --> 01:58:58.345
They're in Badwater.

3270
01:58:58.345 --> 01:58:59.298
I don't know if you noticed this.

3271
01:58:59.298 --> 01:59:01.644
Well, all the kids that work in the restaurants

3272
01:59:01.644 --> 01:59:03.350
in the hotels are all-
Yeah, yeah.

3273
01:59:03.350 --> 01:59:04.248
From strange foreign countries

3274
01:59:04.248 --> 01:59:05.928
doing their like year abroad.

3275
01:59:05.928 --> 01:59:07.133
And I'm like, you got sent here?

3276
01:59:07.133 --> 01:59:08.061
Right.

3277
01:59:08.061 --> 01:59:09.912
This is your American experience,

3278
01:59:09.912 --> 01:59:13.028
like stuck in the middle of the desert at age 19.

3279
01:59:13.028 --> 01:59:14.066
Yeah, yeah.

3280
01:59:14.066 --> 01:59:15.566
Like what do you guys do all day

3281
01:59:15.566 --> 01:59:16.399
when you're not working?

3282
01:59:16.399 --> 01:59:17.534
Well, it's a you know,

3283
01:59:17.534 --> 01:59:19.533
and Badwater is a great race for a lot of reasons.

3284
01:59:19.533 --> 01:59:21.271
It's certainly are very difficult race,

3285
01:59:21.271 --> 01:59:24.607
but it is like most big ultras.

3286
01:59:24.607 --> 01:59:27.368
It's a family, you go to Western states,

3287
01:59:27.368 --> 01:59:29.528
you go to Leadville any of these,

3288
01:59:29.528 --> 01:59:32.942
you tend to see the same people generally over and over.

3289
01:59:32.942 --> 01:59:35.536
And it's this big celebration,

3290
01:59:35.536 --> 01:59:39.395
really of something difficult and interesting and beautiful.

3291
01:59:39.395 --> 01:59:43.007
And for no reason that's been taken away for this year.

3292
01:59:43.007 --> 01:59:44.324
I mean, literally for no reason.

3293
01:59:44.324 --> 01:59:46.734
And hopefully, people will,

3294
01:59:46.734 --> 01:59:50.357
at least write to the right appropriate people

3295
01:59:50.357 --> 01:59:51.653
and complain.

3296
01:59:51.653 --> 01:59:55.092
But anyway, to my race this past year, I went there.

3297
01:59:55.092 --> 01:59:57.577
Chris gave me the race number two.

3298
01:59:57.577 --> 01:59:59.705
Like he assigned to me, number two,

3299
01:59:59.705 --> 02:00:02.155
And usually race numbers are assigned

3300
02:00:02.155 --> 02:00:03.994
based on your previous years finished.

3301
02:00:03.994 --> 02:00:05.092
Previous years finished, yeah.

3302
02:00:05.092 --> 02:00:07.898
So obviously that wasn't the case for me.

3303
02:00:07.898 --> 02:00:09.495
So I don't actually know this,

3304
02:00:09.495 --> 02:00:11.998
but I assume whoever was second the year before

3305
02:00:11.998 --> 02:00:12.915
didn't come

3306
02:00:14.887 --> 02:00:15.761
last year,

3307
02:00:15.761 --> 02:00:18.408
otherwise they would've been assigned number two.

3308
02:00:18.408 --> 02:00:22.379
So whoever that was didn't make it in the last year,

3309
02:00:22.379 --> 02:00:23.964
so he gave me number two,

3310
02:00:23.964 --> 02:00:27.718
which to me instantly put like tons of extra pressure,

3311
02:00:27.718 --> 02:00:30.681
like there was some expectation.

3312
02:00:30.681 --> 02:00:32.149
And in fact, somebody before the race,

3313
02:00:32.149 --> 02:00:34.784
I overheard a comment that someone made,

3314
02:00:34.784 --> 02:00:35.617
a woman made that,

3315
02:00:35.617 --> 02:00:37.414
that I didn't deserve number two.

3316
02:00:37.414 --> 02:00:38.587
She didn't know I could hear her.

3317
02:00:38.587 --> 02:00:39.420
Oh, wow.

3318
02:00:39.420 --> 02:00:40.469
Yeah, and so I was like,

3319
02:00:40.469 --> 02:00:43.642
I will admit to sort of going, grr, okay.

3320
02:00:43.642 --> 02:00:46.153
But I really went there with a,

3321
02:00:46.153 --> 02:00:48.903
I think a good conservative plan.

3322
02:00:49.938 --> 02:00:51.343
I went there to win the race though.

3323
02:00:51.343 --> 02:00:53.681
I would never have said that out loud

3324
02:00:53.681 --> 02:00:56.043
and never will before a race,

3325
02:00:56.043 --> 02:00:59.366
but in my mind, that's the mindset that I,

3326
02:00:59.366 --> 02:01:00.199
I had to have.

3327
02:01:00.199 --> 02:01:03.084
And I was fortunate enough to run a time that

3328
02:01:03.084 --> 02:01:04.815
that actually was fast enough to win

3329
02:01:04.815 --> 02:01:06.640
a whole lot of the years in the past.

3330
02:01:06.640 --> 02:01:08.373
Right, and break the masters record.

3331
02:01:08.373 --> 02:01:09.206
Correct?
Yeah.

3332
02:01:09.206 --> 02:01:12.694
Yeah, I actually broke it by three hours and had a,

3333
02:01:12.694 --> 02:01:15.527
if there's any such thing as an easy race at Badwater,

3334
02:01:15.527 --> 02:01:18.650
I certainly had the easiest one I had ever had.

3335
02:01:18.650 --> 02:01:20.560
I saw you a couple times,

3336
02:01:20.560 --> 02:01:22.060
you didn't look like it was easy.

3337
02:01:22.060 --> 02:01:22.893
(Charlie laughing)

3338
02:01:22.893 --> 02:01:23.726
You didn't look like,

3339
02:01:23.726 --> 02:01:24.559
you didn't look relaxed.
[Charlie] Really?

3340
02:01:24.559 --> 02:01:25.566
You do not look relaxed.

3341
02:01:25.566 --> 02:01:26.768
Dang it, that's-

3342
02:01:26.768 --> 02:01:27.729
Yeah, really bad.
(Charlie laughing)

3343
02:01:27.729 --> 02:01:29.901
But you were killing it the whole time.

3344
02:01:29.901 --> 02:01:31.013
I was happy to see you.

3345
02:01:31.013 --> 02:01:32.176
That's 'cause there's stuff.

3346
02:01:32.176 --> 02:01:33.009
I remember what's the?

3347
02:01:33.009 --> 02:01:35.363
Is it what's the town where you come in

3348
02:01:35.363 --> 02:01:37.769
and you get all the ice.

3349
02:01:37.769 --> 02:01:39.050
Well, there's stove pipe.

3350
02:01:39.050 --> 02:01:40.052
I think a stove pipe.

3351
02:01:40.052 --> 02:01:40.885
Yeah.

3352
02:01:40.885 --> 02:01:41.718
It was like three in the afternoon

3353
02:01:41.718 --> 02:01:42.551
when the heat was really dialed in.

3354
02:01:42.551 --> 02:01:44.042
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

3355
02:01:44.042 --> 02:01:45.158
I saw you,

3356
02:01:45.158 --> 02:01:47.669
I was getting ice for Dean and I saw you coming through

3357
02:01:47.669 --> 02:01:48.807
and you ran into the bushes

3358
02:01:48.807 --> 02:01:50.076
to go to the bathroom or something like that

3359
02:01:50.076 --> 02:01:50.985
and running by.

3360
02:01:50.985 --> 02:01:53.481
And I was like, wow, you're really up there, man.

3361
02:01:53.481 --> 02:01:55.875
You were killing it, but you didn't look like you,

3362
02:01:55.875 --> 02:01:57.952
it wasn't like, you're like smiling and waving.

3363
02:01:57.952 --> 02:01:58.785
Yeah.

3364
02:01:58.785 --> 02:01:59.618
You know what I mean?

3365
02:01:59.618 --> 02:02:00.886
Like it was really hot.

3366
02:02:00.886 --> 02:02:03.293
Well, my crew and Astacianna,

3367
02:02:03.293 --> 02:02:04.637
I was really just trying to impress.

3368
02:02:04.637 --> 02:02:05.470
(Rich laughing)

3369
02:02:05.470 --> 02:02:06.303
I was really just trying to impress her.

3370
02:02:06.303 --> 02:02:07.635
She's laughing over that.

3371
02:02:07.635 --> 02:02:08.614
That's the only thing I was trying to do

3372
02:02:08.614 --> 02:02:09.447
was to impress her.

3373
02:02:09.447 --> 02:02:11.113
So I had to look good.
(Astacianna laughing)

3374
02:02:11.113 --> 02:02:11.946
Right.

3375
02:02:11.946 --> 02:02:14.633
But the fact is I do,

3376
02:02:14.633 --> 02:02:16.172
my crew always knows that I actually,

3377
02:02:16.172 --> 02:02:19.291
I joke the whole time and I, even if I'm miserable,

3378
02:02:19.291 --> 02:02:22.541
I do enjoy the experience tremendously,

3379
02:02:23.639 --> 02:02:25.128
and I like being out there.

3380
02:02:25.128 --> 02:02:27.579
But this year, I don't know.

3381
02:02:27.579 --> 02:02:28.503
Two things happened,

3382
02:02:28.503 --> 02:02:30.300
I think that that made me have a great race.

3383
02:02:30.300 --> 02:02:32.407
Maybe three, if I just count

3384
02:02:32.407 --> 02:02:34.736
having an awesome girlfriend at the time,

3385
02:02:34.736 --> 02:02:38.537
but she taught me how to hydrate properly,

3386
02:02:38.537 --> 02:02:41.215
which it sounds like a funny thing but-

3387
02:02:41.215 --> 02:02:42.216
Yeah, for a guy who,

3388
02:02:42.216 --> 02:02:44.327
the guy who ran across the Sahara Desert-

3389
02:02:44.327 --> 02:02:45.160
Yeah.

3390
02:02:45.160 --> 02:02:45.993
Needs to be told how to hydrate.

3391
02:02:45.993 --> 02:02:46.993
Well, I used to show up

3392
02:02:46.993 --> 02:02:48.392
in Death Valley every year

3393
02:02:48.392 --> 02:02:52.081
and I'd maybe start drinking extra water a few days before.

3394
02:02:52.081 --> 02:02:54.394
And certainly, when I got out into that dryness

3395
02:02:54.394 --> 02:02:56.350
and hotness, I'd ramp it up.

3396
02:02:56.350 --> 02:02:57.183
The fact is,

3397
02:02:57.183 --> 02:03:00.358
what I figured out was my dehydration was chronic.

3398
02:03:00.358 --> 02:03:03.108
And that as a runner, I'm almost,

3399
02:03:04.308 --> 02:03:06.837
I never had done a great job,

3400
02:03:06.837 --> 02:03:09.236
so a couple months before that race.

3401
02:03:09.236 --> 02:03:10.635
I really thanks to her,

3402
02:03:10.635 --> 02:03:13.206
started focusing on hydration.

3403
02:03:13.206 --> 02:03:15.814
The other honestly is it was the shoes,

3404
02:03:15.814 --> 02:03:17.664
I actually switched to Hokas

3405
02:03:17.664 --> 02:03:22.195
and I had run in some fantastic shoe brands before

